(16, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 5, 'A bag contains 24 oranges. If 3/4 of them are given away, how many oranges remain?', 'Medium', '', '', 'Word Problem', '3/4 of 24 is 18 oranges given away. Subtracting from 24 leaves 6 oranges remaining.', 'approved', 0, 2, 0, 57, '2026-06-12 14:23:14', '2026-06-12 14:24:03', 0, 0),
(17, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 5, 'Which of these fractions is larger: 2/3 or 3/5?', 'Medium', '', '', 'Comparison', 'Convert to decimals: 2/3 ≈ 0.666 and 3/5 = 0.6. Alternatively, cross-multiply: 2×5=10 vs 3×3=9. The larger product (10) corresponds to 2/3.', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 57, '2026-06-12 14:23:14', '2026-06-12 14:23:54', 0, 0),
(18, 2, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 English - Item 1 - Question 1</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 English - Question 1</strong></p><p>Choose the option that is most nearly opposite in meaning to the underlined word and that will correctly fill the gap in the sentence.</p><p>The <u>posh</u> cars were sandwiched between two ______ ones.</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Antonyms', '', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-13 16:21:07', NULL, 0, 2025),
(19, 2, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 English - Item 2 - Question 2</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 English - Question 2</strong></p><p>Choose the option that is most nearly opposite in meaning to the underlined word and that will correctly fill the gap in the sentence.</p><p>A <u>trivial</u> issue often becomes ______ when it is not properly handled.</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Antonyms', '', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-13 16:21:07', NULL, 0, 2025),
(20, 2, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 English - Item 3 - Question 3</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 English - Question 3</strong></p><p>Choose the option that is most nearly opposite in meaning to the underlined word and that will correctly fill the gap in the sentence.</p><p>The rockstar&#039;s <u>stellar</u> performance contrasted sharply with the ______ showing of the amateur group.</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Antonyms', '', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-13 16:21:07', NULL, 0, 2025),
(21, 2, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 English - Item 4 - Question 4</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 English - Question 4</strong></p><p>Choose the option that is most nearly opposite in meaning to the underlined word and that will correctly fill the gap in the sentence.</p><p>Tolu was <u>sanctioned</u> for late-coming but his friend was ______.</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Antonyms', '', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-13 16:21:07', NULL, 0, 2025),
(22, 2, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 English - Item 5 - Question 5</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 English - Question 5</strong></p><p>Choose the option that is most nearly opposite in meaning to the underlined word and that will correctly fill the gap in the sentence.</p><p>While other teachers&#039; support for the action ______, Victor&#039;s was <u>dogged</u>.</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Antonyms', '', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-13 16:21:07', NULL, 0, 2025),
(23, 2, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 English - Item 6 - Question 6</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 English - Question 6</strong></p><p>Choose the option that is most nearly opposite in meaning to the underlined word and that will correctly fill the gap in the sentence.</p><p>Some people are good at <u>terminating</u> other people&#039;s projects but are not capable of ______ theirs.</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Antonyms', '', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-13 16:21:07', NULL, 0, 2025),
(24, 2, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 English - Item 7 - Question 7</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 English - Question 7</strong></p><p>Choose the option that is most nearly opposite in meaning to the underlined word and that will correctly fill the gap in the sentence.</p><p>The <u>precarious</u> terraces of the stadium have been transformed into a ______ walkway.</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Antonyms', '', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-13 16:21:07', NULL, 0, 2025),
