(318, 2, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2024 English - Item 1 - Question 1</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2024 English - Question 1</strong></p><p>In each of the following sentences, there is one underlined word and one gap. From the list of words lettered A to D, choose the one that is <strong>most nearly opposite</strong> in meaning to the underlined word and that will, at the same time, correctly fill the gap in the sentence.<br>Abdul&#39;s contribution at the meeting was seen by many as <u>invaluable</u> but the chairman said it was _________</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Antonyms', '', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 12:12:48', NULL, 0, 2024),
(319, 2, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2024 English - Item 2 - Question 2</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2024 English - Question 2</strong></p><p>In each of the following sentences, there is one underlined word and one gap. From the list of words lettered A to D, choose the one that is <strong>most nearly opposite</strong> in meaning to the underlined word and that will, at the same time, correctly fill the gap in the sentence.<br>The boy may be <u>culpable</u> but his brother is surely ______.</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Antonyms', '', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 12:12:48', NULL, 0, 2024),
(320, 2, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2024 English - Item 3 - Question 3</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2024 English - Question 3</strong></p><p>In each of the following sentences, there is one underlined word and one gap. From the list of words lettered A to D, choose the one that is <strong>most nearly opposite</strong> in meaning to the underlined word and that will, at the same time, correctly fill the gap in the sentence<br>Our class teacher used to be <u>rigid</u> in his opinions but he is now ______ of other people&#39;s views</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Antonyms', '', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 12:12:49', NULL, 0, 2024),
(321, 2, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2024 English - Item 4 - Question 4</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2024 English - Question 4</strong></p><p>In each of the following sentences, there is one underlined word and one gap. From the list of words lettered A to D, choose the one that is <strong>most nearly opposite</strong> in meaning to the underlined word and that will, at the same time, correctly fill the gap in the sentence.<br>Some workers were quite <u>affable</u> at the meeting but their leader was rather ______</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Antonyms', '', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 12:12:49', NULL, 0, 2024),
(322, 2, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2024 English - Item 5 - Question 5</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2024 English - Question 5</strong></p><p>In each of the following sentences, there is one underlined word and one gap. From the list of words lettered A to D, choose the one that is <strong>most nearly opposite</strong> in meaning to the underlined word and that will, at the same time, correctly fill the gap in the sentence.<br>The driver believed he would be <u>castigated</u> by all the passengers but he was ______.</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Antonyms', '', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 12:12:49', NULL, 0, 2024),
(323, 2, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2024 English - Item 6 - Question 6</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2024 English - Question 6</strong></p><p>In each of the following sentences, there is one underlined word and one gap. From the list of words lettered A to D, choose the one that is <strong>most nearly opposite</strong> in meaning to the underlined word and that will, at the same time, correctly fill the gap in the sentence.<br>The manager was <u>eulogised</u> for his speech while his assistant was ________</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Antonyms', '', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 12:12:49', NULL, 0, 2024),
(324, 2, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2024 English - Item 7 - Question 7</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2024 English - Question 7</strong></p><p>In each of the following sentences, there is one underlined word and one gap. From the list of words lettered A to D, choose the one that is <strong>most nearly opposite</strong> in meaning to the underlined word and that will, at the same time, correctly fill the gap in the sentence.<br>Some people are <u>generous</u> towards strangers, while others are _______ towards them.</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Antonyms', '', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 12:12:49', NULL, 0, 2024),
(325, 2, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2024 English - Item 8 - Question 8</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2024 English - Question 8</strong></p><p>In each of the following sentences, there is one underlined word and one gap. From the list of words lettered A to D, choose the one that is <strong>most nearly opposite</strong> in meaning to the underlined word and that will, at the same time, correctly fill the gap in the sentence.<br>The baby who had all along been <u>calm</u> suddenly became _________</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Antonyms', '', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 12:12:49', NULL, 0, 2024),
(326, 2, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2024 English - Item 9 - Question 9</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2024 English - Question 9</strong></p><p>In each of the following sentences, there is one underlined word and one gap. From the list of words lettered A to D, choose the one that is <strong>most nearly opposite</strong> in meaning to the underlined word and that will, at the same time, correctly fill the gap in the sentence.</p><p>While Ade is ______, his wife is quite <u>self-effacing</u>.</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Antonyms', '', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 12:12:49', NULL, 0, 2024),
(327, 2, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2024 English - Item 10 - Question 10</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2024 English - Question 10</strong></p><p>In each of the following sentences, there is one underlined word and one gap. From the list of words lettered A to D, choose the one that is <strong>most nearly opposite</strong> in meaning to the underlined word and that will, at the same time, correctly fill the gap in the sentence.<br>Bakary is a <u>prudent</u> husband while Musa is ______.</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Antonyms', '', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 12:12:49', NULL, 0, 2024),
(328, 2, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2024 English - Item 11 - Question 11</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2024 English - Question 11</strong></p><p><em>From the words lettered A-D, choose the word that <strong>best completes </strong>each of the following sentences.</em><br>The incumbent chairman won the election by a ______ of twenty votes.</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Sentence Completion', '', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 12:12:49', NULL, 0, 2024),
(329, 2, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2024 English - Item 12 - Question 12</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2024 English - Question 12</strong></p><p><em>From the words lettered A-D, choose the word that <strong>best completes </strong>each of the following sentences.</em><br>Since all items on the agenda had been discussed, the meeting was _______.</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Sentence Completion', '', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 12:12:49', NULL, 0, 2024),
(330, 2, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2024 English - Item 13 - Question 13</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2024 English - Question 13</strong></p><p><em>From the words lettered A-D, choose the word that <strong>best completes </strong>each of the following sentences.</em><br>The police explained that all the aggrieved persons should seek _______ in the court of law.</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Sentence Completion', '', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 12:12:49', NULL, 0, 2024),
