INSERT INTO `question_bank` (`id`, `subject_id`, `class_id`, `source_type`, `exam_body_id`, `topic_id`, `question`, `difficulty`, `recommended_class`, `term_tag`, `question_category`, `explanation`, `review_status`, `quality_score`, `times_used`, `school_id`, `createdby`, `datecreated`, `dateupdated`, `deleted`, `exam_year`) VALUES
(460, 47, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Economics - Item 1 - Question 1</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Economics - Question 1</strong></p><p>The study of economics is important to every society because it</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Economics', '<p>Economics is the study of how societies, governments, businesses, households, and individuals allocate their scarce resources. It<br>helps in the utilization of scarce resources by determining what to produce, how to produce, and for whom to produce. The other<br>options are not entirely correct because economics does not enable individuals to satisfy all their wants due to the concept of<br>scarcity, it does not directly help producers to know what to produce, and it does not restore equilibrium between producers and<br>consumers.</p>', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 15:57:05', NULL, 0, 2025),
(461, 47, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Economics - Item 2 - Question 2</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Economics - Question 2</strong></p><p>A consumer with $10 needs a dress, a pair of shoes, a handbag and jewellery costing $20, $10, $7 and $3 respectively. The</p><p>opportunity cost of buying the pair of shoes is the</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Economics', '<p>Opportunity cost in economics refers to the value of the</p>', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 15:57:05', NULL, 0, 2025),
(462, 47, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Economics - Item 3 - Question 3</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Economics - Question 3</strong></p><p>The distinguishing function of an entrepreneur is</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Production', '<p>The distinguishing function of an entrepreneur is risk-bearing. Entrepreneurs are individuals who, rather than working as an<br>employee, found and run small businesses, assuming all the risks and rewards of the venture. The other options such as planning,<br>control, and management are functions that can be performed by managers and do not specifically distinguish an entrepreneur.</p>', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 15:57:05', NULL, 0, 2025),
(463, 47, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Economics - Item 4 - Question 4</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Economics - Question 4</strong></p><p>When a commodity market operates without government interference, commodities are distributed through</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Demand and Supply', '<p>In a free market economy, where there is no government interference, commodities are distributed through the operation of price<br>mechanism. The price mechanism is a system where the forces of supply and demand interact to determine the price of a<br>commodity. When demand for a commodity is high, the price increases and when the supply of a commodity is high, the price<br>decreases.</p>', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 15:57:05', NULL, 0, 2025),
(464, 47, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Economics - Item 5 - Question 5</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Economics - Question 5</strong></p><p>One way of obtaining the median of a given data is to</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Economic Calculations', '<p>The median of a given data set is the middle value when the data is arranged in either ascending or descending order. If the data<br>set has an odd number of observations, the median is the middle value. If the data set has an even number of observations, the<br>median is the average of the two middle values.</p>', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 15:57:05', NULL, 0, 2025),
(465, 47, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Economics - Item 6 - Question 6</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Economics - Question 6</strong></p><p>An increase in rice harvest, all things being equal, may cause</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Demand and Supply', '<p>In economics, when the supply of a commodity increases, all other things being equal, the price of the commodity tends to fall.<br>This is because the increased supply creates a surplus in the market, which puts downward pressure on the price. Therefore, an<br>increase in rice harvest would likely cause the price of rice to fall substantially.</p>', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 15:57:05', NULL, 0, 2025),
(466, 47, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Economics - Item 7 - Question 7</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Economics - Question 7</strong></p><p>The demand for wood and labour is an example of</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Demand and Supply', '<p>The demand for wood and labour is an example of derived demand. Derived demand refers to the demand for goods and services<br>that arises not for its own sake but due to the demand for another good or service. For instance, the demand for wood and labour<br>arises due to the demand for furniture, construction, etc.</p>', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 15:57:05', NULL, 0, 2025),
(467, 47, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Economics - Item 8 - Question 8</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Economics - Question 8</strong></p><p>What will be the reaction of consumers in a market if there is a fall in the price of the substitute of commodity X?</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Demand and Supply', '<p>If there is a fall in the price of the substitute of commodity X, consumers will likely switch to the substitute because it&#39;s now<br>cheaper. This will cause the demand for commodity X to decrease.</p>', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 15:57:05', NULL, 0, 2025),
(468, 47, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Economics - Item 9 - Question 9</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Economics - Question 9</strong></p><p>An increase in market supply is caused by the following factors except</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Demand and Supply', '<p>An increase in the price of the commodity does not cause an increase in market supply. In fact, it&#39;s the opposite. An increase in the<br>price of a commodity can lead to an increase in the quantity supplied (as suppliers are willing to supply more at higher prices),<br>but it does not shift the supply curve or increase market supply. The other options (improvement in innovation and technology,<br>reduction in the cost of raw materials, and favourable weather conditions) can all lead to an increase in market supply.</p>', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 15:57:05', NULL, 0, 2025),
(469, 47, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Economics - Item 10 - Question 10</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Economics - Question 10</strong></p><p>The coefficient of price elasticity of supply of land is usually</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Economic Calculations', '<p>The coefficient of price elasticity of supply of land is usually zero. This is because the supply of land is perfectly inelastic, meaning<br>it does not respond to changes in price. The quantity of land is fixed and cannot be increased or decreased in response to changes<br>in price.</p>', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 15:57:05', NULL, 0, 2025),
(470, 47, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Economics - Item 11 - Question 11</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Economics - Question 11</strong></p><p>The price of soap rose from $10 to $20, causing a trader to increase her supply from 50 to 120 boxes per week. This makes supply</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Economic Calculations', '<p>The price elasticity of supply can be calculated using the formula: % change in quantity supplied / % change in price. In this case,<br>the % change in quantity supplied is (120-50)/50 = 1.4 and the % change in price is (20-10)/10 = 1. Therefore, the price elasticity<br>of supply is 1.4/1 = 1.4, which is greater than 1. This means the supply is fairly elastic, meaning that the quantity supplied is<br>responsive to changes in price.</p>', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 15:57:05', NULL, 0, 2025),
(471, 47, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Economics - Item 12 - Question 12</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Economics - Question 12</strong></p><p>A leftward shift in the supply curve for a commodity indicates</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Demand and Supply', '<p>A leftward shift in the supply curve for a commodity indicates a decrease in supply. This could be due to a number of factors such<br>as an increase in production costs, a decrease in technology, or a decrease in the number of suppliers. This shift means that at<br>every price level, the quantity supplied is less than before.</p>', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 15:57:05', NULL, 0, 2025),
(472, 47, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Economics - Item 13 - Question 13</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Economics - Question 13</strong></p><p>Market supply may increase if there is an increase in the</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Demand and Supply', '<p>Subsidies on raw materials reduce the cost of production, encouraging producers to produce more, hence increasing the market<br>supply.</p>', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 15:57:05', NULL, 0, 2025),
(473, 47, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Economics - Item 14 - Question 14</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Economics - Question 14</strong></p><p>Governments can increase farmers&#39; incomes by</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Market Structure and Business', '<p>Fixing minimum prices ensures that farmers receive a certain amount of income for their products, regardless of the market<br>conditions.</p>', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 15:57:06', NULL, 0, 2025),
(474, 47, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Economics - Item 15 - Question 15</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Economics - Question 15</strong></p><p>When market supply increases, the equilibrium price</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Demand and Supply', '<p>An increase in supply, with demand remaining constant, leads to a surplus in the market. This surplus puts downward pressure on<br>the price until it falls to a level where the quantity supplied equals the quantity demanded, i.e., the equilibrium point.</p>', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 15:57:06', NULL, 0, 2025),
(475, 47, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Economics - Item 16 - Question 16</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Economics - Question 16</strong></p><p>The supply of mangoes is represented as P = 0.3Q, where P is the price ($) and Q is the quantity. What is P when Q is 50?</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Demand and Supply', '<p>The supply of mangoes is represented as P = 0.3Q. To find the price (P) when the quantity (Q) is 50, we substitute Q = 50 into the<br>equation. This gives P = 0.3 * 50 = $15.00. Therefore, the correct answer is $15.00.</p>', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 15:57:06', NULL, 0, 2025),
(476, 47, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Economics - Item 17 - Question 17</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Economics - Question 17</strong></p><p>The output of an extra unit of input is referred to as</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Economics', '<p>The output of an extra unit of input is referred to as the marginal product of the input. This is a concept in economics that<br>describes the additional output that can be produced by adding one more unit of a specific input, while holding all other inputs<br>constant. Therefore, the correct answer is &#39;marginal product of the input&#39;.</p>', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 15:57:06', NULL, 0, 2025),
(477, 47, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Economics - Item 18 - Question 18</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Economics - Question 18</strong></p><p>The law of diminishing returns is applicable to the</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Production', '<p>The law of diminishing returns, also known as the law of variable proportions, states that if one input in the production of a<br>commodity is increased while all other inputs are held fixed, a point will eventually be reached at which additions of the input<br>yield progressively smaller, or diminishing, increases in output. This law is applicable to the variable factors of production.<br>Therefore, the correct answer is &#39;variable factors of production&#39;.</p>', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 15:57:06', NULL, 0, 2025),
(478, 47, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Economics - Item 19 - Question 19</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Economics - Question 19</strong></p><p>A firm incurred the following costs in production. Use the information in the table to answer questions below</p><p>Output(bags of rice) | 0 | 10 | 20 | 30 | 40 | 50 | 60<br>Total cost$ | 100 | 200 | 300 | 380 | 440 | 520 | 600</p><p>The fixed cost of production is</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Production', '<p>Fixed cost is the cost that does not change with the level of output. It is the cost incurred even when the output is zero. From the<br>table, when the output is zero, the total cost is $100. Therefore, the fixed cost of production is $100.</p>', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 15:57:06', NULL, 0, 2025),
(479, 47, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Economics - Item 20 - Question 20</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Economics - Question 20</strong></p><p>A firm incurred the following costs in production. Use the information in the table to answer questions below</p><p>Output(bags of rice) | 0 | 10 | 20 | 30 | 40 | 50 | 60<br>Total cost$ | 100 | 200 | 300 | 380 | 440 | 520 | 600</p><p>The average cost of producing 40 bags of rice is</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Economic Calculations', '<p>Average cost is calculated by dividing the total cost by the quantity of output. From the table, the total cost of producing 40 bags<br>of rice is $440. Therefore, the average cost of producing 40 bags of rice is $440/40 = $11.</p>', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 15:57:06', NULL, 0, 2025),
(480, 47, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Economics - Item 21 - Question 21</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Economics - Question 21</strong></p><p>The relationship between the marginal revenue (MR) and the average revenue (AR) of a monopolist is that the marginal revenue</p><p>curve</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Economics', '<p>In a monopoly, the marginal revenue (MR) curve is always below the average revenue (AR) curve and slopes downwards. This is<br>because a monopolist can only sell more by lowering the price, which reduces both the average revenue and the marginal revenue.</p>', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 15:57:06', NULL, 0, 2025),
(481, 47, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Economics - Item 22 - Question 22</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Economics - Question 22</strong></p><p>A major source of finance to the Railway Corporation in West African countries is</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Economics', '<p>The major source of finance for the Railway Corporation in West African countries is government subvention. Government<br>subvention refers to the financial aid or support that a government provides to a particular entity or a group of entities. In this<br>case, the government provides financial support to the Railway Corporation to ensure its smooth operation and maintenance.</p>', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 15:57:06', NULL, 0, 2025),
(482, 47, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Economics - Item 23 - Question 23</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Economics - Question 23</strong></p><p>Separation of ownership of resources and their control is mostly found in a</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Economics', '<p>The separation of ownership of resources and their control is mostly found in a joint stock company. In a joint stock company, the<br>shareholders are the owners of the company but the control is in the hands of the board of directors. The shareholders have<br>limited liability and they are not involved in the day-to-day operations of the company.</p>', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 15:57:06', NULL, 0, 2025),
(483, 47, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Economics - Item 24 - Question 24</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Economics - Question 24</strong></p><p>By-passing the middlemen in the chain of distribution can lead to</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Population and Labour', '<p>By-passing the middlemen in the chain of distribution can lead to a problem of unemployment of labour. Middlemen play a crucial<br>role in the distribution of goods and services from producers to consumers. If they are bypassed, it could lead to unemployment<br>as these middlemen would lose their jobs. This is because the role they play in the distribution chain would be eliminated.</p>', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 15:57:06', NULL, 0, 2025),
(484, 47, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Economics - Item 25 - Question 25</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Economics - Question 25</strong></p><p>Two factors which can improve the efficiency of labour are</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Population and Labour', '<p>The efficiency of labour can be improved by enhancing the work environment and the health status of workers. A conducive work<br>environment can boost the morale and productivity of workers. Similarly, a healthy worker is more likely to be productive than<br>an unhealthy one. Therefore, the correct answer is option 3.</p>', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 15:57:06', NULL, 0, 2025),
(485, 47, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Economics - Item 26 - Question 26</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Economics - Question 26</strong></p><p>The age distribution of a country&#39;s population is shown below. Use the information to answer questions below</p><p>AGE GROUP (YEARS) | POPULATION<br>0-15 | 30%<br>16-40 | 45%<br>41-60 | 15%<br>Over 60 | 10%</p><p>What is the percentage of the working population?</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Economic Calculations', '<p>16 - 40 and 41 - 60 are working population.<br>i.e. 45 + 15 = 60%</p>', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 15:57:06', NULL, 0, 2025),
(486, 47, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Economics - Item 27 - Question 27</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Economics - Question 27</strong></p><p>The age distribution of a country&#39;s population is shown below. Use the information to answer questions below</p><p>AGE GROUP (YEARS) | POPULATION<br>0-15 | 30%<br>16-40 | 45%<br>41-60 | 15%<br>Over 60 | 10%</p><p>What is the dependency ratio?</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Population and Labour', '<p>Dependent population = Dependent pop / Independent pop<br>Dependent pop = 30 + 10 = 40<br>Independent pop = 45 + 15 = 60<br>Dep pop = 40/60</p><p>=2:3</p>', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 15:57:06', NULL, 0, 2025),
(487, 47, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Economics - Item 28 - Question 28</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Economics - Question 28</strong></p><p>The supply of land for agricultural purpose can be increased through</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Demand and Supply', '<p>The supply of land for agricultural purposes can be increased through reclamation and irrigation. Reclamation refers to the<br>process of creating new land from oceans, riverbeds, or lake beds, while irrigation involves the application of controlled amounts<br>of water to plants at needed intervals. Both processes can help increase the amount of land available for agricultural purposes.</p>', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 15:57:06', NULL, 0, 2025),
(488, 47, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Economics - Item 29 - Question 29</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Economics - Question 29</strong></p><p>Non-economic factors that influence the location of firms include</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Economics', '<p>Non-economic factors that influence the location of firms include the activities of politicians in deciding the location of firms.<br>This is because political factors such as government policies, regulations, and political stability can significantly influence where<br>a firm chooses to locate its operations.</p>', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 15:57:06', NULL, 0, 2025),
(489, 47, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Economics - Item 30 - Question 30</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Economics - Question 30</strong></p><p>Which of the following is not an argument for the policy of privatization in West Africa?</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Market Structure and Business', '<p>The statement &#39;Government is able to participate and control the operation of the privatized businesses&#39; is not an argument for<br>the policy of privatization in West Africa. Privatization is the process of transferring an enterprise or industry from the public<br>sector to the private sector. The main idea behind this process is to allow for greater private sector participation and reduce<br>government involvement in the economy.</p>', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 15:57:06', NULL, 0, 2025),
(490, 47, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Economics - Item 31 - Question 31</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Economics - Question 31</strong></p><p>The following data relates to the national income of a country.</p><p>Gross domestic product = $2800</p><p>Net factor income from abroad =$250</p><p>Depreciation = $700</p><p>Indirect taxes = $120 Use it to answer questions 31 and 32 What is the country&#39;s Gross National Product (GNP)?</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Economic Calculations', '<p>Gross National Product (GNP) is calculated by adding the Gross Domestic Product (GDP) and the Net Factor Income from Abroad.<br>So, GNP = GDP + Net Factor Income from Abroad = $2800 + $250 = $3050.</p>', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 15:57:06', NULL, 0, 2025),
(491, 47, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Economics - Item 32 - Question 32</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Economics - Question 32</strong></p><p>What is the country&#39;s Net National Product (NNP) at factor cost?</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Economic Calculations', '<p>Net National Product (NNP) at factor cost is calculated by subtracting Depreciation and Indirect taxes from the GNP. So, NNP at<br>factor cost = GNP - Depreciation - Indirect taxes = $3050 - $700-$120 = $2230.</p>', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 15:57:06', NULL, 0, 2025),
(492, 47, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Economics - Item 33 - Question 33</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Economics - Question 33</strong></p><p>The standard of living in two countries can be compared using the</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Economics', '<p>The standard of living in two countries can be compared using the Gross National Product per head. This is because it gives the<br>average income of a citizen in a country, which is a good indicator of the standard of living.</p>', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 15:57:06', NULL, 0, 2025),
(493, 47, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Economics - Item 34 - Question 34</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Economics - Question 34</strong></p><p>Government can curb inflation by</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Demand and Supply', '<p>Inflation can be curbed by the government by selling securities in the open market. This is because when the government sells<br>securities, it reduces the amount of money in circulation, which in turn reduces the demand for goods and services, thereby<br>reducing inflation. This is a monetary policy tool known as open market operations.</p>', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 15:57:06', NULL, 0, 2025),
(494, 47, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Economics - Item 35 - Question 35</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Economics - Question 35</strong></p><p>Functions of money does not include</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Money and Banking', '<p>The functions of money are:<br>- store of value<br>- standard of deferred payment<br>- medium of exchange<br>- unit of account</p>', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 15:57:06', NULL, 0, 2025),
(495, 47, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Economics - Item 36 - Question 36</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Economics - Question 36</strong></p><p>Demand -Pull inflation can be as a result of</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Demand and Supply', '<p>Demand-Pull inflation can be a result of deficit financing by the government. Deficit financing refers to the government&#39;s spending<br>more than it collects in revenue. This increases the demand for goods and services, which can lead to inflation if the supply does<br>not keep up with the demand.</p>', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 15:57:06', NULL, 0, 2025),
(496, 47, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Economics - Item 37 - Question 37</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Economics - Question 37</strong></p><p>An increase in cash ratio by the central bank will</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Demand and Supply', '<p>The cash ratio is a measure of a bank&#39;s liquidity and ability to meet its obligations. An increase in the cash ratio by the central<br>bank means that banks are required to hold more reserves and thus, they have less money to lend out. This reduces the supply of<br>money in the economy.</p>', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 15:57:06', NULL, 0, 2025),
(497, 47, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Economics - Item 38 - Question 38</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Economics - Question 38</strong></p><p>When the government cuts down her expenditure to reduce inflation, she has embarked on</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Money and Banking', '<p>A restrictive fiscal policy is a type of policy that is used to combat inflation. It involves reducing government spending and/or<br>increasing taxes. This reduces the amount of money in circulation, which can help to reduce inflation. Therefore, when the<br>government cuts down her expenditure to reduce inflation, she has embarked on a restrictive fiscal policy.</p>', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 15:57:06', NULL, 0, 2025),
(498, 47, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Economics - Item 39 - Question 39</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Economics - Question 39</strong></p><p>In order to enable the government of a country to increase its tax revenue, it will be advisable for it to increase taxes on</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Demand and Supply', '<p>Inelastic demand refers to a situation where the demand for a product does not change significantly with changes in price.<br>Therefore, increasing taxes on goods with inelastic demand, such as alcoholic beverages, would not significantly affect their<br>consumption but would increase the government&#39;s tax revenue.</p>', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 15:57:06', NULL, 0, 2025),
(499, 47, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Economics - Item 40 - Question 40</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Economics - Question 40</strong></p><p>People who dispose of their assets are expected to pay</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Money and Banking', '<p>People who dispose of their assets are expected to pay capital gains tax. Capital gains tax is a tax on the profit when you sell (or<br>&#39;dispose of&#39;) something (an &#39;asset&#39;) that&#39;s increased in value. It&#39;s the gain you make that&#39;s taxed, not the amount of money you<br>receive.</p>', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 15:57:06', NULL, 0, 2025),
(500, 47, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Economics - Item 41 - Question 41</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Economics - Question 41</strong></p><p>A floating exchange rate means that the exchange rate is fixed by the</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Demand and Supply', '<p>A floating exchange rate means that the exchange rate is determined by the forces of demand and supply. In a floating exchange<br>rate system, when the demand for a currency is low, its value decreases just as with any other product or service. But when the<br>demand is high, the value increases.</p>', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 15:57:06', NULL, 0, 2025),
(501, 47, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Economics - Item 42 - Question 42</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Economics - Question 42</strong></p><p>A measure that can be adopted to correct a country&#39;s balance of payments deficit is to</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Production', '<p>A measure that can be adopted to correct a country&#39;s balance of payments deficit is to adopt import substitution strategy. Import<br>substitution industrialization (ISI) is a trade and economic policy which advocates replacing foreign imports with domestic<br>production. It is based on the premise that a country should attempt to reduce its foreign dependency through the local<br>production of industrialized products.</p>', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 15:57:06', NULL, 0, 2025),
(502, 47, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Economics - Item 43 - Question 43</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Economics - Question 43</strong></p><p>Records of a country&#39;s invisible trade are recorded in her</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'International Trade', '<p>Invisible trade refers to the trading of services and other non-tangible goods, which are recorded in the current account of a<br>country&#39;s balance of payments. The current account includes transactions in goods, services, income, and current transfers.</p>', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 15:57:06', NULL, 0, 2025),
(503, 47, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Economics - Item 44 - Question 44</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Economics - Question 44</strong></p><p>If a country&#39;s import bill is high, she can encourage exports by</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Demand and Supply', '<p>When a country&#39;s currency depreciates, its goods and services become cheaper for foreign buyers, which can increase demand for<br>its exports.</p>', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 15:57:06', NULL, 0, 2025),
(504, 47, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Economics - Item 45 - Question 45</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Economics - Question 45</strong></p><p>If a country&#39;s imposes a barrier on trade, the resultant effect will be</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Demand and Supply', '<p>Trade barriers, such as tariffs and quotas, make imported goods more expensive, which can increase demand for cheaper, locally<br>produced goods.</p>', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 15:57:06', NULL, 0, 2025),
(505, 47, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Economics - Item 46 - Question 46</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Economics - Question 46</strong></p><p>A country may be able to earn more from exports if she</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Market Structure and Business', '<p>Devaluing a country&#39;s currency can make its exports cheaper and more attractive to foreign buyers, potentially leading to an<br>increase in export earnings. This is because when a country devalues its currency, the price of its goods and services decreases in<br>terms of foreign currency, making them more competitive in the global market.</p>', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 15:57:06', NULL, 0, 2025),
(506, 47, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Economics - Item 47 - Question 47</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Economics - Question 47</strong></p><p>A customs union is an economic grouping which has</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'International Trade', '<p>A customs union is a type of trade bloc which is composed of a free trade area with a common external tariff. The participant<br>countries set up common external trade policy, but in some cases they use different import quotas. Common competition policy is<br>also helpful to avoid competition deficiency.</p>', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 15:57:06', NULL, 0, 2025),
(507, 47, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Economics - Item 48 - Question 48</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Economics - Question 48</strong></p><p>Balance of payments and trade problems that arose after the world wars were resolved by the</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'International Trade', '<p>The International Monetary Fund (IMF) was created in 1944 to help manage and stabilize the global monetary system,<br>particularly in the aftermath of World War II. It provides financial assistance to countries facing balance of payments problems,<br>helping to stabilize international exchange rates and facilitate global trade.</p>', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 15:57:06', NULL, 0, 2025),
(508, 47, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Economics - Item 49 - Question 49</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Economics - Question 49</strong></p><p>Examples of land that are non-renewable include</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Economics', '<p>Land in economics refers to all naturally occurring resources. Natural gas is a naturally occurring resource that is non-renewable<br>because once it is used, it cannot be replenished. Therefore, it is an example of non-renewable land.</p>', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 15:57:06', NULL, 0, 2025),
(509, 47, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Economics - Item 50 - Question 50</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Economics - Question 50</strong></p><p>Abundant natural resources do not contribute to economic growth in developing countries because of</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Economic Development', '<p>Abundant natural resources do not contribute to economic growth in developing countries mainly due to mismanagement and<br>corruption. These factors prevent the efficient use and allocation of these resources, thereby hindering economic growth.</p><p>============================================================</p><p>END OF QUESTION BANK ??? 50 Questions</p><p>EXTRACTION SUMMARY</p><p>- Total pages processed: 12<br>- Total questions extracted: 58 (50 Objective + 8 Theory)<br>- Objective questions in this document: 50<br>- Theory questions (excluded): 8 (Questions 51-58)<br>- Questions with correct answers: 50<br>- Questions with explanations: 50<br>- Questions containing tables/data: 4 (Questions 19, 20, 26, 27)<br>- No images found in objective questions<br>- No pages required retries<br>- Question numbering: Sequential 1-50 (no duplicates, no skips)</p>', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 15:57:06', NULL, 0, 2025),
(560, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Item 1 - Question 1</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Question 1</strong></p><p>Find <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"(101₂)\"></span>², expressing the answer in base 2.</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Number and Logarithms', '', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 22:10:25', NULL, 0, 2025),
(561, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Item 2 - Question 2</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Question 2</strong></p><p>If three children share ₦10.50 among themselves in the ratio 6:7:8, how much is the largest share?</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Commercial Mathematics', '', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 22:10:25', NULL, 0, 2025),
(562, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Item 3 - Question 3</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Question 3</strong></p><p>Express 0.000834 in standard form.</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Number and Logarithms', '', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 22:10:25', NULL, 0, 2025),
(563, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Item 4 - Question 4</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Question 4</strong></p><p>Simplify 0.<span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"027\\frac{-1}{3}\"></span></p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Mathematics', '', 'approved', 0, 2, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 22:10:25', NULL, 0, 2025),
(564, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Item 5 - Question 5</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Question 5</strong></p><p>Given that <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"log_{2}a =\"></span><span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"log_{84}\"></span>, find a.</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Number and Logarithms', '', 'approved', 0, 2, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 22:10:25', NULL, 0, 2025),
(565, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Item 6 - Question 6</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Question 6</strong></p><p>By selling some crates of soft drinks for ₦600.00, a dealer makes a profit of 50%. How much did the dealer pay for the drinks?</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Commercial Mathematics', '', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 22:10:25', NULL, 0, 2025),
(566, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Item 7 - Question 7</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Question 7</strong></p><p>Find the nth term Un of the A.P. 11, 4, -3, …</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Sequences and Series', '', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 22:10:25', NULL, 0, 2025),
(567, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Item 8 - Question 8</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Question 8</strong></p><p>If <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"R = {2, 4, 6, 7}\"></span> and <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"S = {1, 2, 4, 8}\"></span> then <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"R \\cup S\"></span> equals</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Sets', '', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 22:10:25', NULL, 0, 2025),
(568, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Item 9 - Question 9</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Question 9</strong></p><p>If <br><span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"\\frac{16}{9}\"></span><br>, x, 1, y are in geometric progression (G.P.). Find the product of x and y.</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Sequences and Series', '', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 22:10:25', NULL, 0, 2025),
(569, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Item 10 - Question 10</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Question 10</strong></p><p><img src=\"../uploads/question_bank/waec_2025_mathematics/Q10_diagram.png\" alt=\"Diagram for WAEC 2025 Mathematics Question 10\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;\"></p><p>In the diagram above, the shaded portion is</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Mathematics', '', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 22:10:25', NULL, 0, 2025),
(570, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Item 11 - Question 11</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Question 11</strong></p><p>Find the values of x for which the expression is undefined: <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"(6 \\times - 1)\"></span>/<span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"( \\times ^{2} + 4 \\times - 5)\"></span></p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Algebra', '', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 22:10:25', NULL, 0, 2025),
(571, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Item 12 - Question 12</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Question 12</strong></p><p>Solve the inequality <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"\\frac{1}{3}\"></span><span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"(2 \\times - 1)\"></span> &lt; 5</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Algebra', '', 'approved', 0, 2, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 22:10:25', NULL, 0, 2025),
(572, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Item 13 - Question 13</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Question 13</strong></p><p>What is the smaller value of x for which <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"\\times ^{2} - 3 \\times + 2 = 0\"></span> ?</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Mathematics', '', 'approved', 0, 2, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 22:10:25', NULL, 0, 2025),
(573, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Item 14 - Question 14</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Question 14</strong></p><p>Factorize the expression x<span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"(a - c)\"></span> + y<span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"(c - a)\"></span></p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Algebra', '', 'approved', 0, 2, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 22:10:25', NULL, 0, 2025),
(574, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Item 15 - Question 15</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Question 15</strong></p><p>If y <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"\\propto\"></span> 1⁄x² and x = 3, when y = 4, find y when x = 2</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Mathematics', '', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 22:10:25', NULL, 0, 2025),
(575, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Item 16 - Question 16</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Question 16</strong></p><p>Solve the equation <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"3 \\times ^{2} + 25 \\times - 18\"></span> = 0</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Algebra', '', 'approved', 0, 2, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 22:10:25', NULL, 0, 2025),
(576, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Item 17 - Question 17</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Question 17</strong></p><p>Solve the equation <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"( \\times + 2)\"></span><span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"( \\times - 7)\"></span> = 0</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Algebra', '', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 22:10:25', NULL, 0, 2025),
(577, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Item 18 - Question 18</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Question 18</strong></p><p>Solve the following simultaneous equations: x + y = <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"\\frac{3}{2}\"></span>, x - y = <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"\\frac{5}{2}\"></span>. And use your result to find the value of 2y + x.</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Algebra', '', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 22:10:25', NULL, 0, 2025),
(578, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Item 19 - Question 19</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Question 19</strong></p><p><img src=\"../uploads/question_bank/waec_2025_mathematics/Q19_diagram.png\" alt=\"Diagram for WAEC 2025 Mathematics Question 19\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;\"></p><p>Which of the following could be the inequality illustrated in the sketch graph above?</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Algebra', '', 'approved', 0, 2, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 22:10:25', NULL, 0, 2025),
(579, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Item 20 - Question 20</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Question 20</strong></p><p><img src=\"../uploads/question_bank/waec_2025_mathematics/Q20_diagram.png\" alt=\"Diagram for WAEC 2025 Mathematics Question 20\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;\"></p><p>What is the minimum value of y?</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Mathematics', '', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 22:10:25', NULL, 0, 2025),
(580, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Item 21 - Question 21</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Question 21</strong></p><p><img src=\"../uploads/question_bank/waec_2025_mathematics/Q21_diagram.png\" alt=\"Diagram for WAEC 2025 Mathematics Question 21\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;\"></p><p>Find the roots of the equation y = <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"3 \\times ^{2} + \\times - 7\"></span>.</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Algebra', '', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 22:10:25', NULL, 0, 2025),
(581, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Item 22 - Question 22</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Question 22</strong></p><p>The diagonals AC and BD of a rhombus ABCD are 16 cm and 12 cm long, respectively. Calculate the area of the rhombus.</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Geometry', '', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 22:10:26', NULL, 0, 2025),
(582, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Item 23 - Question 23</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Question 23</strong></p><p><img src=\"../uploads/question_bank/waec_2025_mathematics/Q23_diagram.png\" alt=\"Diagram for WAEC 2025 Mathematics Question 23\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;\"></p><p>A cylindrical container, closed at both ends, has a radius of 7 cm and a height of 5 cm. Use this information to answer the questions below. Find the total surface area of the container.</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Mensuration', '', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 22:10:26', NULL, 0, 2025),
(583, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Item 24 - Question 24</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Question 24</strong></p><p>Find the total surface area of a solid circular cone with base radius 3 cm and slant height 4 cm. [Take <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"\\pi\"></span> = <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"\\frac{22}{7}\"></span>]</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Mensuration', '', 'approved', 0, 2, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 22:10:26', NULL, 0, 2025),
(584, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Item 25 - Question 25</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Question 25</strong></p><p>A water tank of height <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"\\frac{1}{2}\"></span> m has a square base of side <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"1\\frac{1}{2}\"></span>m. If it is filled with water from a water tanker holding 1500 litres, how many litres of water are left in the water tanker? [1000 litres = 1 m³]</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Commercial Mathematics', '', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 22:10:26', NULL, 0, 2025),
(585, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Item 26 - Question 26</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Question 26</strong></p><p>A hollow sphere has a volume of k cm³ and a surface area of k cm². Calculate the diameter of the sphere.</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Mensuration', '', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 22:10:26', NULL, 0, 2025),
(586, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Item 27 - Question 27</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Question 27</strong></p><p><img src=\"../uploads/question_bank/waec_2025_mathematics/Q27_diagram.png\" alt=\"Diagram for WAEC 2025 Mathematics Question 27\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;\"></p><p>The diagram above shows a cone with the dimensions of its frustum indicated. Calculate the height of the cone.</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Mensuration', '', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 22:10:26', NULL, 0, 2025),
(587, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Item 28 - Question 28</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Question 28</strong></p><p>The positions of two countries, P and Q, are (<span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"15^{\\circ}\"></span>N, <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"12^{\\circ}\"></span>E) and (<span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"65^{\\circ}\"></span>N, <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"12^{\\circ}\"></span>E) respectively. What is the difference in latitude?</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Bearing and Earth Geometry', '', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 22:10:26', NULL, 0, 2025),
(588, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Item 29 - Question 29</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Question 29</strong></p><p>A <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"120^{\\circ}\"></span> sector of a circle of radius 21 cm is bent to form a cone. What is the base radius of the cone?</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Mensuration', '', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 22:10:26', NULL, 0, 2025),
(589, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Item 30 - Question 30</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Question 30</strong></p><p><img src=\"../uploads/question_bank/waec_2025_mathematics/Q30_diagram.png\" alt=\"Diagram for WAEC 2025 Mathematics Question 30\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;\"></p><p>A cylindrical container, closed at both ends, has a radius of 7 cm and a height of 5 cm. Use this information to answer the questions below. What is the volume of the container?</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Mensuration', '', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 22:10:26', NULL, 0, 2025);
INSERT INTO `question_bank` (`id`, `subject_id`, `class_id`, `source_type`, `exam_body_id`, `topic_id`, `question`, `difficulty`, `recommended_class`, `term_tag`, `question_category`, `explanation`, `review_status`, `quality_score`, `times_used`, `school_id`, `createdby`, `datecreated`, `dateupdated`, `deleted`, `exam_year`) VALUES
(590, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Item 31 - Question 31</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Question 31</strong></p><p>If <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"log_{10} \\times = 2.3675\"></span> and <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"log_{10}y = 2.9738\"></span>, what is the value of x + y, correct to three significant figures</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Number and Logarithms', 'The source appears to omit barred-log notation. Answer uses the barred characteristic interpretation, giving x + y ≈ 0.117.', 'approved', 0, 2, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 22:10:26', NULL, 0, 2025),
(591, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Item 32 - Question 32</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Question 32</strong></p><p>The angle of a sector of a circle is <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"108 ^{\\circ}\"></span>. If the radius of the circle is <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"3\\frac{1}{2}\"></span>cm, find the perimeter of the sector.</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Mensuration', '', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 22:10:26', NULL, 0, 2025),
(592, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Item 33 - Question 33</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Question 33</strong></p><p><img src=\"../uploads/question_bank/waec_2025_mathematics/Q33_diagram.png\" alt=\"Diagram for WAEC 2025 Mathematics Question 33\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;\"></p><p>In the diagram above, AO is perpendicular to OB. Find x.</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Mathematics', '', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 22:10:26', NULL, 0, 2025),
(593, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Item 34 - Question 34</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Question 34</strong></p><p><img src=\"../uploads/question_bank/waec_2025_mathematics/Q34_diagram.png\" alt=\"Diagram for WAEC 2025 Mathematics Question 34\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;\"></p><p>In the diagram above. O is the centre of the circle and |BD| = |DC|. If ∠DCB = <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"35^{\\circ}\"></span>, find ∠BAO</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Mathematics', '', 'approved', 0, 3, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 22:10:26', NULL, 0, 2025),
(594, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Item 35 - Question 35</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Question 35</strong></p><p>Which of the following angles is an exterior angle of a regular polygon?</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Geometry', '', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 22:10:26', NULL, 0, 2025),
(595, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Item 36 - Question 36</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Question 36</strong></p><p>The locus of a point which is equidistant from two given fixed points is the</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Geometry', '', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 22:10:26', NULL, 0, 2025),
(596, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Item 37 - Question 37</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Question 37</strong></p><p><img src=\"../uploads/question_bank/waec_2025_mathematics/Q37_diagram.png\" alt=\"Diagram for WAEC 2025 Mathematics Question 37\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;\"></p><p>In the diagram,|AB| = 12cm, |AE| = 8cm, |DC| = 9cm and BD||DC. Find the length of EC.</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Mathematics', '', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 22:10:26', NULL, 0, 2025),
(597, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Item 38 - Question 38</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Question 38</strong></p><p><img src=\"../uploads/question_bank/waec_2025_mathematics/Q38_diagram.png\" alt=\"Diagram for WAEC 2025 Mathematics Question 38\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;\"></p><p>In the diagram above, PQ is parallel to TU, ∠PQR = <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"50^{\\circ}\"></span>, ∠QRS = <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"86^{\\circ}\"></span>, and ∠STU = <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"64^{\\circ}\"></span>. Calculate the value of x</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Mathematics', '', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 22:10:26', NULL, 0, 2025),
(598, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Item 39 - Question 39</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Question 39</strong></p><p><img src=\"../uploads/question_bank/waec_2025_mathematics/Q39_diagram.png\" alt=\"Diagram for WAEC 2025 Mathematics Question 39\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;\"></p><p>In the diagram below, AB||DC, the bisectors of ∠BAC and ∠ACD meet at E. Find the value of ∠AEC</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Mensuration', '', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 22:10:26', NULL, 0, 2025),
(599, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Item 40 - Question 40</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Question 40</strong></p><p><img src=\"../uploads/question_bank/waec_2025_mathematics/Q40_diagram.png\" alt=\"Diagram for WAEC 2025 Mathematics Question 40\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;\"></p><p>In the diagram above, AB||CD. What is the size of the angle marked x?</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Geometry', '', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 22:10:26', NULL, 0, 2025),
(600, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Item 41 - Question 41</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Question 41</strong></p><p><img src=\"../uploads/question_bank/waec_2025_mathematics/Q41_diagram.png\" alt=\"Diagram for WAEC 2025 Mathematics Question 41\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;\"></p><p>In the diagram above, the value of angles b + c is</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Geometry', '', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 22:10:26', NULL, 0, 2025),
(601, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Item 42 - Question 42</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Question 42</strong></p><p><img src=\"../uploads/question_bank/waec_2025_mathematics/Q42_diagram.png\" alt=\"Diagram for WAEC 2025 Mathematics Question 42\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;\"></p><p>In △ABC above, BC is produced to D, |AB| = |AC|, and ∠BAC = <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"50^{\\circ}\"></span>. Find ∠ACD.</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Mathematics', '', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 22:10:26', NULL, 0, 2025),
(602, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Item 43 - Question 43</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Question 43</strong></p><p><img src=\"../uploads/question_bank/waec_2025_mathematics/Q43_diagram.png\" alt=\"Diagram for WAEC 2025 Mathematics Question 43\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;\"></p><p>In the diagram above, ∠PRQ = <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"90^{\\circ}\"></span>, ∠QPR = <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"30^{\\circ}\"></span> and |PQ| = 10 cm. Find y</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Mathematics', '', 'approved', 0, 3, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 22:10:26', NULL, 0, 2025),
(603, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Item 44 - Question 44</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Question 44</strong></p><p>What is the mode of the numbers 8, 10, 9, 9, 10, 8, 11, 8, 10, 9, 8, and 14?</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Statistics', '', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 22:10:26', NULL, 0, 2025),
(604, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Item 45 - Question 45</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Question 45</strong></p><p>The bearing of two points Q and R from a point P are <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"030^{\\circ}\"></span> and <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"120^{\\circ}\"></span>, respectively. If |PQ| = 12 m and |PR| = 5 m, find the distance QR.</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Bearing and Earth Geometry', '', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 22:10:26', NULL, 0, 2025),
(605, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Item 46 - Question 46</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Question 46</strong></p><p>Without using tables, find the value of: <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"sin 20^{\\circ}/cos 70^{\\circ} + cos 25^{\\circ}/sin 65^{\\circ}\"></span></p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Trigonometry', '', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 22:10:26', NULL, 0, 2025),
(606, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Item 47 - Question 47</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Question 47</strong></p><p>The mean of 20 observations in an experiment is 4. If the observed largest value is 23, find the mean of the remaining observations.</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Statistics', '', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 22:10:26', NULL, 0, 2025),
(607, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Item 48 - Question 48</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Question 48</strong></p><p>Two fair dice are tossed together once. Find the probability that the sum of the outcomes is at least 10.</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Probability', '', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 22:10:26', NULL, 0, 2025),
(608, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Item 49 - Question 49</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Question 49</strong></p><p>Find the median of the following numbers: 2.64, 2.50, 2.72, 2.91, and 2.35</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Statistics', '', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 22:10:26', NULL, 0, 2025),
(609, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Item 50 - Question 50</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Mathematics - Question 50</strong></p><p>From a box containing 2 red, 6 white, and 5 black balls, a ball is randomly selected. What is the probability that the selected ball is black?</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Probability', '', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 22:10:26', NULL, 0, 2025),
(610, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Item 1 - Question 1</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Question 1</strong></p><p>Multiply 3.4 x 10⁻⁵ by 7.1 x 10⁸ and leave the answer in standard form.</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Number and Logarithms', '', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 23:51:28', NULL, 0, 2024),
(611, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Item 2 - Question 2</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Question 2</strong></p><p>Given that P = {p: 1&lt; p &lt; 20}, where p is an integer and R = {r : 0 ≤ r ≤ 25, where r is a multiple of 4}. Find P ∩ R</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Sets', '', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 23:51:28', NULL, 0, 2024),
(612, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Item 3 - Question 3</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Question 3</strong></p><p>The first term of an Arithmetic Progression (A.P) is 2 and the last term is 29. If the common difference is 3, how many terms are in the A.P.?</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Sequences and Series', '', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 23:51:28', NULL, 0, 2024),
(613, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Item 4 - Question 4</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Question 4</strong></p><p>Express in index form: <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"log_x a + log_y a = 3\"></span></p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Logarithms', '', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 23:51:28', NULL, 0, 2024),
(614, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Item 5 - Question 5</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Question 5</strong></p><p>Simplify: <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"(2p - q)^2 - (p + q)^2\"></span></p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Algebra', '', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 23:51:28', NULL, 0, 2024),
(615, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Item 6 - Question 6</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Question 6</strong></p><p>If <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"(3 - 4\\sqrt{2})(1 + 3\\sqrt{2}) = a + b\\sqrt{2}\"></span>, find the value of <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"b\"></span>.</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Surds', '', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 23:51:28', NULL, 0, 2024),
(616, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Item 7 - Question 7</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Question 7</strong></p><p>Find the sum for which ₦ 1,250.00 will amount to ₦ 2,031.25 at 12.5% per annum simple interest.</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Commercial Mathematics', '', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 23:51:28', NULL, 0, 2024),
(617, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Item 8 - Question 8</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Question 8</strong></p><p>If <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"log_3(2x - 1) = 5\"></span>, find the value of <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"x\"></span>.</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Logarithms', '', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 23:51:28', NULL, 0, 2024),
(618, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Item 9 - Question 9</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Question 9</strong></p><p>The population of a town increases by 3% every year. In the year 2000, the population was 3000. Find the population in the year 2003.</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Commercial Mathematics', '', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 23:51:28', NULL, 0, 2024),
(619, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Item 10 - Question 10</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Question 10</strong></p><p>A trader gave a change of ₦ 540.00 instead of ₦ 570.00 to a customer. Calculate the percentage error.</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Approximation and Percentage', '', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 23:51:28', NULL, 0, 2024),
(620, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Item 11 - Question 11</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Question 11</strong></p><p>The interior angle of a regular polygon is 168°. Find the number of sides of the polygon.</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Geometry', '', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 23:51:28', NULL, 0, 2024),
(621, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Item 12 - Question 12</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Question 12</strong></p><p>If <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"3x - 2y = -5\"></span> and <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"x + 2y = 9\"></span>, find the value of <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"\\frac{x-y}{x+y}\"></span>.</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Algebraic Fractions', '', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 23:51:28', NULL, 0, 2024),
(622, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Item 13 - Question 13</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Question 13</strong></p><p>A variable <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"W\"></span> varies partly as <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"M\"></span> and partly inversely as <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"P\"></span>. Which of the following correctly represents the relation with <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"k_1\"></span> and <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"k_2\"></span> as constants?</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Variation', '', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 23:51:28', NULL, 0, 2024),
(623, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Item 14 - Question 14</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Question 14</strong></p><p>A cylindrical metallic barrel of height 2.5 m and radius 0.245 m is closed at one end. Find, correct to one decimal place, the total surface area of the barrel. Take <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"\\pi = \\frac{22}{7}\"></span>.</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Mensuration', '', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 23:51:28', NULL, 0, 2024),
(624, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Item 15 - Question 15</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Question 15</strong></p><p>Make <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"R\"></span> the subject of the relation <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"V = \\pi l(R^2 - r^2)\"></span>.</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Change of Subject', '', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 23:51:28', NULL, 0, 2024),
(625, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Item 16 - Question 16</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Question 16</strong></p><p>Consider the following statements: m = Edna is respectful n = Edna is brilliant, If m ⇒ n, which of the following is valid?</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Logic', '', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 23:51:28', NULL, 0, 2024),
(626, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Item 17 - Question 17</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Question 17</strong></p><p>A number is added to both the numerator and the denominator of the fraction <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"\\frac{1}{8}\"></span>. If the result is <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"\\frac{1}{2}\"></span>, find the number.</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Algebra', '', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 23:51:28', NULL, 0, 2024),
(627, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Item 18 - Question 18</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Question 18</strong></p><p>Gifty, Justina, and Frank shared 60 oranges in the ratio 5: 3: 7 respectively. How many oranges did Justina receive?</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Ratio', '', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 23:51:28', NULL, 0, 2024),
(628, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Item 19 - Question 19</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Question 19</strong></p><p>Find the quadratic equation whose roots are <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"\\frac{2}{3}\"></span> and <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"-1\"></span>.</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Quadratic Equations', '', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 23:51:28', NULL, 0, 2024),
(629, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Item 20 - Question 20</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Question 20</strong></p><p>A piece of rod of length 44 m is cut to form a rectangular shape such that the ratio of the length to the breadth is 7: 4. Find the breadth.</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Mensuration', '', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 23:51:28', NULL, 0, 2024),
(630, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Item 21 - Question 21</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Question 21</strong></p><p><img src=\"../uploads/question_bank/waec_2024_mathematics/Q21_diagram.png\" alt=\"Diagram for WAEC 2024 Mathematics Question 21\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;\"></p><p>In the diagram above, <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"\\overline{MN} \\parallel \\overline{KL}\"></span>, <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"\\overline{ML}\"></span> and <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"\\overline{KN}\"></span> intersect at <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"X\"></span>. If <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"|MN| = 12\\text{ cm}\"></span>, <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"|KL| = 9\\text{ cm}\"></span>, <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"|MX| = 10\\text{ cm}\"></span> and the area of <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"\\triangle MXN\"></span> is <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"16\\text{ cm}^2\"></span>, calculate the area of <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"\\triangle LXK\"></span>.</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Geometry', '', 'approved', 0, 2, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 23:51:28', NULL, 0, 2024),
(631, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Item 22 - Question 22</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Question 22</strong></p><p>A ladder 15 m long leans against a vertical pole, making an angle of 72° with the horizontal. Calculate, correct to one decimal place, the distance between the foot of the ladder and the pole.</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Trigonometry', '', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 23:51:28', NULL, 0, 2024),
(632, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Item 23 - Question 23</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Question 23</strong></p><p><img src=\"../uploads/question_bank/waec_2024_mathematics/Q23_diagram.png\" alt=\"Diagram for WAEC 2024 Mathematics Question 23\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;\"></p><p>In the diagram above, <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"O\"></span> is the centre of the circle. If <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"|OA| = 25\\text{ cm}\"></span> and <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"|AB| = 40\\text{ cm}\"></span>, find <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"|OH|\"></span>.</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Circle Geometry', '', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 23:51:28', NULL, 0, 2024),
(633, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Item 24 - Question 24</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Question 24</strong></p><p>A car valued at ₦ 600,000.00 depreciates by 10% each year. What will be the value of the car at the end of two years?</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Commercial Mathematics', '', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 23:51:28', NULL, 0, 2024),
(634, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Item 25 - Question 25</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Question 25</strong></p><p>Given that P is 25 m on a bearing of 330° from Q, how far south of P is Q?</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Bearings', '', 'approved', 0, 2, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 23:51:28', NULL, 0, 2024),
(635, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Item 26 - Question 26</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Question 26</strong></p><p>The length and breadth of a cuboid are 15 cm and 8 cm respectively. If the volume of the cuboid is 1560 cm³, calculate the total surface area.</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Mensuration', '', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 23:51:28', NULL, 0, 2024),
(636, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Item 27 - Question 27</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Question 27</strong></p><p>The number <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"1621_x\"></span> was subtracted from <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"6244_x\"></span>. If the result was <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"4323_x\"></span>, find <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"x\"></span>.</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Number Bases', '', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 23:51:28', NULL, 0, 2024),
(637, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Item 28 - Question 28</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Question 28</strong></p><p>Factorize completely: <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"27x^2 - 48y^2\"></span>.</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Algebra', '', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 23:51:28', NULL, 0, 2024),
(638, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Item 29 - Question 29</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Question 29</strong></p><p>For what values of <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"x\"></span> is <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"\\frac{x-3}{4} + \\frac{x+1}{8} \\ge 2\"></span>?</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Linear Inequalities', '', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 23:51:28', NULL, 0, 2024),
(639, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Item 30 - Question 30</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Question 30</strong></p><p><img src=\"../uploads/question_bank/waec_2024_mathematics/Q30_diagram.png\" alt=\"Diagram for WAEC 2024 Mathematics Question 30\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;\"></p><p>In the diagram above, <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"\\angle SQR = 52^{\\circ}\"></span> and <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"\\angle PRT = 16^{\\circ}\"></span>. Find the value of the angle marked <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"y\"></span>.</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Circle Geometry', '', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 23:51:28', NULL, 0, 2024),
(640, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Item 31 - Question 31</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Question 31</strong></p><p><img src=\"../uploads/question_bank/waec_2024_mathematics/Q31_diagram.png\" alt=\"Diagram for WAEC 2024 Mathematics Question 31\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;\"></p><p>In the diagram above, <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"JKL\"></span> is a tangent to the circle <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"GHIK\"></span> at <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"K\"></span>. Find the value of the angle marked <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"x\"></span>.</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Circle Geometry', '', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 23:51:28', NULL, 0, 2024),
(641, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Item 32 - Question 32</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Question 32</strong></p><p>A cone and a cylinder are of equal volume. The base radius of the cone is twice the radius of the cylinder. What is the ratio of the height of the cylinder to that of the cone?</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Mensuration', '', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 23:51:28', NULL, 0, 2024),
(642, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Item 33 - Question 33</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Question 33</strong></p><p><img src=\"../uploads/question_bank/waec_2024_mathematics/Q33_diagram.png\" alt=\"Diagram for WAEC 2024 Mathematics Question 33\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;\"></p><p>Find, correct to the nearest ​​​​​​whole number, the value of h in the diagram above.</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Trigonometry', '', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 23:51:28', NULL, 0, 2024),
(643, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Item 34 - Question 34</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Question 34</strong></p><p>The gradient of the line joining the points P(2, -8) and Q(1, y) is -4. Find the value of y</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Coordinate Geometry', '', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 23:51:28', NULL, 0, 2024),
(644, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Item 35 - Question 35</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Question 35</strong></p><p><img src=\"../uploads/question_bank/waec_2024_mathematics/Q35_diagram.png\" alt=\"Diagram for WAEC 2024 Mathematics Question 35\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;\"></p><p>In the diagram above, <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"PQ \\parallel RS\"></span>, <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"\\angle WYZ = 44^{\\circ}\"></span> and <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"\\angle WXY = 50^{\\circ}\"></span>. Find <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"\\angle WTX\"></span>.</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Angles and Parallel Lines', '', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 23:51:28', NULL, 0, 2024),
(645, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Item 36 - Question 36</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Question 36</strong></p><p>The perimeter of a rectangular garden is 90 m. If the width is 7 m less than the length, find the length of the garden.</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Algebra', '', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 23:51:28', NULL, 0, 2024),
(646, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Item 37 - Question 37</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Question 37</strong></p><p>Four of the angles of a hexagon sum up to <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"420^{\\circ}\"></span>. If the remaining angles are equal, find the value of each of the angles.</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Polygons', '', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 23:51:28', NULL, 0, 2024),
(647, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Item 38 - Question 38</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Question 38</strong></p><p><img src=\"../uploads/question_bank/waec_2024_mathematics/Q38_diagram.png\" alt=\"Diagram for WAEC 2024 Mathematics Question 38\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;\"></p><p>Find the value of x in the diagram above.</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Geometry', '', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 23:51:28', NULL, 0, 2024),
(648, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Item 39 - Question 39</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Question 39</strong></p><p>The following are the masses (in kg) of members in a club: 59, 44, 53, 49, 57, 40, 48, and 50. Calculate the mean mass.</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Statistics', '', 'approved', 0, 2, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 23:51:28', NULL, 0, 2024),
(649, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Item 40 - Question 40</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Question 40</strong></p><p>The following are the masses (in kg) of members in a club: 59, 44, 53, 49, 57, 40, 48, and 50. Calculate the variance of the distribution.</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Statistics', '', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 23:51:28', NULL, 0, 2024),
(650, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Item 41 - Question 41</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Question 41</strong></p><p>Two opposite sides of a rectangle are (5x + 3) m and (2x + 9) m. If an adjacent side is (6x - 7) m, find in m², the area of the rectangle.</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Algebra', '', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 23:51:28', NULL, 0, 2024),
(651, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Item 42 - Question 42</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Question 42</strong></p><p>A die is tossed once. Find the probability of getting a prime number.</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Probability', '', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 23:51:28', NULL, 0, 2024),
(652, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Item 43 - Question 43</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Question 43</strong></p><p>The area of a sector of a circle with radius 7 cm is <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"51.3\\text{ cm}^2\"></span>. Calculate, correct to the nearest whole number, the angle of the sector. Take <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"\\pi = \\frac{22}{7}\"></span>.</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Mensuration', '', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 23:51:28', NULL, 0, 2024),
(653, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Item 44 - Question 44</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Question 44</strong></p><p>A cliff on the bank of a river 87 m high. A boat on the river is 22 m away from the cliff. Calculate, correct to the nearest degree, the angle of depression of the boat from the top of the cliff.</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Trigonometry', '', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 23:51:28', NULL, 0, 2024),
(654, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Item 45 - Question 45</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Question 45</strong></p><p><img src=\"../uploads/question_bank/waec_2024_mathematics/Q45_diagram.png\" alt=\"Diagram for WAEC 2024 Mathematics Question 45\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;\"></p><p>In the diagram, <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"\\overline{TU}\"></span> is a tangent to the circle <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"SPQR\"></span> at <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"P\"></span>. If <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"\\angle PTS = 44^{\\circ}\"></span> and <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"\\angle SQP = 35^{\\circ}\"></span>, find <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"\\angle PST\"></span>.</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Circle Geometry', '', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 23:51:28', NULL, 0, 2024),
(655, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Item 46 - Question 46</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Question 46</strong></p><p>The probability that Amaka will pass an examination is <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"\\frac{3}{7}\"></span> and that Bala will pass is <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"\\frac{4}{9}\"></span>. Find the probability that both will pass the examination.</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Probability', '', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 23:51:28', NULL, 0, 2024),
(656, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Item 47 - Question 47</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Question 47</strong></p><p>Which of the following points lies on the line 3x - 8y = 11?</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Coordinate Geometry', '', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 23:51:28', NULL, 0, 2024),
(657, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Item 48 - Question 48</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Question 48</strong></p><p>Find the range of the following set of numbers: 28, 29, 39, 38, 33, 37, 26, 20, 15, and 25.</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Statistics', '', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 23:51:28', NULL, 0, 2024),
(658, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Item 49 - Question 49</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Question 49</strong></p><p>The fourth and eighth terms of an Arithmetic Progression are 16 and 40 respectively. Find the common difference.</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Sequences and Series', '', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 23:51:28', NULL, 0, 2024),
(659, 1, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Item 50 - Question 50</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2024 Mathematics - Question 50</strong></p><p>For what values of <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"y\"></span> is <span contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"math-editor-rendered\" data-latex=\"\\frac{y + 2}{8y^2 - 10y + 3}\"></span> not defined?</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Algebraic Fractions', '', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-17 23:51:28', NULL, 0, 2024),
(660, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 16, '<p><small>Source: Geometrical Construction Topic Bank - Item 1</small></p><p><strong>Geometrical Construction - Question 1</strong></p><p>Which instrument is mainly used for drawing circles and arcs?</p>', 'Easy', 'JSS3', '', 'Construction Instruments', 'A compass is used to draw circles and arcs.', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 00:24:33', NULL, 0, 0),
(661, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 16, '<p><small>Source: Geometrical Construction Topic Bank - Item 2</small></p><p><strong>Geometrical Construction - Question 2</strong></p><p>Which instrument is used for measuring angles?</p>', 'Easy', 'JSS3', '', 'Construction Instruments', 'A protractor is used to measure angles.', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 00:24:33', NULL, 0, 0),
(662, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 16, '<p><small>Source: Geometrical Construction Topic Bank - Item 3</small></p><p><strong>Geometrical Construction - Question 3</strong></p><p>Which instrument is best used for drawing straight line segments?</p>', 'Easy', 'JSS3', '', 'Construction Instruments', 'A ruler is used for drawing straight lines and measuring lengths.', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 00:24:33', NULL, 0, 0),
(663, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 16, '<p><small>Source: Geometrical Construction Topic Bank - Item 4</small></p><p><strong>Geometrical Construction - Question 4</strong></p><p>A pair of set squares is mainly used to construct</p>', 'Easy', 'JSS3', '', 'Construction Instruments', 'Set squares are commonly used to construct parallel and perpendicular lines.', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 00:24:33', NULL, 0, 0),
(664, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 16, '<p><small>Source: Geometrical Construction Topic Bank - Item 5</small></p><p><strong>Geometrical Construction - Question 5</strong></p><p>The perpendicular bisector of a line segment divides the line segment into</p>', 'Easy', 'JSS3', '', 'Basic Construction', 'A perpendicular bisector cuts a line into two equal parts at 90°.', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 00:24:33', NULL, 0, 0),
(665, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 16, '<p><small>Source: Geometrical Construction Topic Bank - Item 6</small></p><p><strong>Geometrical Construction - Question 6</strong></p><p>An angle bisector divides an angle into</p>', 'Easy', 'JSS3', '', 'Basic Construction', 'An angle bisector divides an angle into two equal angles.', 'approved', 0, 2, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 00:24:33', NULL, 0, 0),
(666, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 16, '<p><small>Source: Geometrical Construction Topic Bank - Item 7</small></p><p><strong>Geometrical Construction - Question 7</strong></p><p>Which of the following angles can be constructed directly using an equilateral triangle?</p>', 'Easy', 'JSS3', '', 'Construction Angles', 'Each angle of an equilateral triangle measures 60°.', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 00:24:33', NULL, 0, 0),
(667, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 16, '<p><small>Source: Geometrical Construction Topic Bank - Item 8</small></p><p><strong>Geometrical Construction - Question 8</strong></p><p>A right angle measures</p>', 'Easy', 'JSS3', '', 'Construction Angles', 'A right angle is 90°.', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 00:24:33', NULL, 0, 0),
(668, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 16, '<p><small>Source: Geometrical Construction Topic Bank - Item 9</small></p><p><strong>Geometrical Construction - Question 9</strong></p><p>How many sides of an equilateral triangle are equal?</p>', 'Easy', 'JSS3', '', 'Triangles', 'All three sides of an equilateral triangle are equal.', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 00:24:33', NULL, 0, 0),
(669, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 16, '<p><small>Source: Geometrical Construction Topic Bank - Item 10</small></p><p><strong>Geometrical Construction - Question 10</strong></p><p>The perpendicular bisector of a line segment is the locus of points that are</p>', 'Easy', 'JSS3', '', 'Locus', 'Every point on a perpendicular bisector is equally distant from the endpoints of the line segment.', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 00:24:33', NULL, 0, 0),
(670, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 16, '<p><small>Source: Geometrical Construction Topic Bank - Item 11</small></p><p><strong>Geometrical Construction - Question 11</strong></p><p>To construct the perpendicular bisector of a line segment, the first step is to</p>', 'Medium', 'JSS3', '', 'Construction Procedure', 'Equal arcs from both endpoints locate points through which the perpendicular bisector passes.', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 00:24:33', NULL, 0, 0),
(671, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 16, '<p><small>Source: Geometrical Construction Topic Bank - Item 12</small></p><p><strong>Geometrical Construction - Question 12</strong></p><p>When constructing the bisector of an angle, the compass radius used for the second pair of arcs should be</p>', 'Medium', 'JSS3', '', 'Construction Procedure', 'Equal radii are required to locate the point through which the angle bisector passes.', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 00:24:33', NULL, 0, 0),
(672, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 16, '<p><small>Source: Geometrical Construction Topic Bank - Item 13</small></p><p><strong>Geometrical Construction - Question 13</strong></p><p>Which set of information is sufficient to construct a unique triangle?</p>', 'Medium', 'JSS3', '', 'Triangles', 'A triangle can be uniquely constructed when all three sides are known (SSS).', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 00:24:33', NULL, 0, 0),
(673, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 16, '<p><small>Source: Geometrical Construction Topic Bank - Item 14</small></p><p><strong>Geometrical Construction - Question 14</strong></p><p>A student uses different compass widths when drawing the two arcs needed to construct a perpendicular bisector. What is the likely result?</p>', 'Medium', 'JSS3', '', 'Error Detection', 'The compass radius must remain the same for both arcs to obtain an accurate perpendicular bisector.', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 00:24:33', NULL, 0, 0),
(674, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 16, '<p><small>Source: Geometrical Construction Topic Bank - Item 15</small></p><p><strong>Geometrical Construction - Question 15</strong></p><p>A surveyor wants to locate a point that is exactly the same distance from two boundary pegs. Which construction should be used?</p>', 'Medium', 'JSS3', '', 'Application', 'Every point on the perpendicular bisector of a line segment is equidistant from its endpoints.', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 00:24:33', NULL, 0, 0),
(675, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 16, '<p><small>Source: Geometrical Construction Topic Bank - Item 16</small></p><p><strong>Geometrical Construction - Question 16</strong></p><p>Which construction is used to draw a line at right angles to a given line from a point on the line?</p>', 'Medium', 'JSS3', '', 'Construction Procedure', 'A perpendicular line meets another line at 90°.', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 00:24:33', NULL, 0, 0),
(676, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 16, '<p><small>Source: Geometrical Construction Topic Bank - Item 17</small></p><p><strong>Geometrical Construction - Question 17</strong></p><p><img src=\"../uploads/question_bank/geometrical_construction/gc_017.png\" alt=\"Diagram for Geometrical Construction Question 17\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;\"></p><p>In the diagram, line PQ passes through the midpoint of AB and meets AB at 90°. What is PQ?</p>', 'Medium', 'JSS3', '', 'Diagram Interpretation', 'A perpendicular bisector cuts a line segment into two equal parts at right angles.', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 00:24:33', NULL, 0, 0),
(677, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 16, '<p><small>Source: Geometrical Construction Topic Bank - Item 18</small></p><p><strong>Geometrical Construction - Question 18</strong></p><p>Which angle can be constructed by bisecting a 90° angle?</p>', 'Medium', 'JSS3', '', 'Construction Angles', 'Half of 90° is 45°.', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 00:24:33', NULL, 0, 0),
(678, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 16, '<p><small>Source: Geometrical Construction Topic Bank - Item 19</small></p><p><strong>Geometrical Construction - Question 19</strong></p><p>Which angle can be constructed by bisecting a 60° angle?</p>', 'Medium', 'JSS3', '', 'Construction Angles', 'Half of 60° is 30°.', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 00:24:33', NULL, 0, 0),
(679, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 16, '<p><small>Source: Geometrical Construction Topic Bank - Item 20</small></p><p><strong>Geometrical Construction - Question 20</strong></p><p>To construct triangle ABC with AB = 6 cm, AC = 5 cm and BC = 4 cm, which construction condition is being used?</p>', 'Medium', 'JSS3', '', 'Triangles', 'All three sides are given, so the triangle is constructed using SSS.', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 00:24:33', NULL, 0, 0),
(680, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 16, '<p><small>Source: Geometrical Construction Topic Bank - Item 21</small></p><p><strong>Geometrical Construction - Question 21</strong></p><p><img src=\"../uploads/question_bank/geometrical_construction/gc_021.png\" alt=\"Diagram for Geometrical Construction Question 21\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;\"></p><p>In the diagram, ray OM divides angle AOB into two equal angles. What is OM?</p>', 'Medium', 'JSS3', '', 'Diagram Interpretation', 'An angle bisector divides an angle into two equal parts.', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 00:24:33', NULL, 0, 0),
(681, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 16, '<p><small>Source: Geometrical Construction Topic Bank - Item 22</small></p><p><strong>Geometrical Construction - Question 22</strong></p><p>When constructing a line parallel to a given line through a point, which pair of instruments is most suitable?</p>', 'Medium', 'JSS3', '', 'Parallel Lines', 'A pair of set squares can be used to draw accurate parallel lines.', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 00:24:33', NULL, 0, 0),
(682, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 16, '<p><small>Source: Geometrical Construction Topic Bank - Item 23</small></p><p><strong>Geometrical Construction - Question 23</strong></p><p>The locus of points at a fixed distance from a given point is</p>', 'Medium', 'JSS3', '', 'Locus', 'All points at a fixed distance from a point form a circle.', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 00:24:33', NULL, 0, 0),
(683, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 16, '<p><small>Source: Geometrical Construction Topic Bank - Item 24</small></p><p><strong>Geometrical Construction - Question 24</strong></p><p>A student wants to construct a 60° angle but draws it using only estimation by eye. What is the main error?</p>', 'Medium', 'JSS3', '', 'Error Detection', 'Geometrical construction requires accurate use of instruments, not guessing by eye.', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 00:24:33', NULL, 0, 0),
(684, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 16, '<p><small>Source: Geometrical Construction Topic Bank - Item 25</small></p><p><strong>Geometrical Construction - Question 25</strong></p><p>A carpenter wants to divide a wooden strip into two equal parts and mark a line at right angles through the middle. Which construction should be used?</p>', 'Medium', 'JSS3', '', 'Application', 'A perpendicular bisector divides a line segment into two equal parts at right angles.', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 00:24:33', NULL, 0, 0),
(685, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 16, '<p><small>Source: Geometrical Construction Topic Bank - Item 26</small></p><p><strong>Geometrical Construction - Question 26</strong></p><p>Which method can be used to construct an angle of 120°?</p>', 'Medium', 'JSS3', '', 'Construction Angles', 'Two successive angles of 60° give 60° + 60° = 120°.', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 00:24:33', NULL, 0, 0),
(686, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 16, '<p><small>Source: Geometrical Construction Topic Bank - Item 27</small></p><p><strong>Geometrical Construction - Question 27</strong></p><p><img src=\"../uploads/question_bank/geometrical_construction/gc_027.png\" alt=\"Diagram for Geometrical Construction Question 27\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;\"></p><p>In the diagram, C and D are equally distant from P on line AB. Arcs drawn from C and D intersect at Q. What is the relationship between PQ and AB?</p>', 'Medium', 'JSS3', '', 'Diagram Interpretation', 'The equal arcs locate Q directly above P, making PQ perpendicular to AB.', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 00:24:33', NULL, 0, 0),
(687, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 16, '<p><small>Source: Geometrical Construction Topic Bank - Item 28</small></p><p><strong>Geometrical Construction - Question 28</strong></p><p>A triangle is to be constructed with one side measuring 7 cm and the two angles at its endpoints measuring 50° and 70°. Which construction condition is used?</p>', 'Medium', 'JSS3', '', 'Triangles', 'Two angles and the included side are given, so the ASA condition is used.', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 00:24:33', NULL, 0, 0);
INSERT INTO `question_bank` (`id`, `subject_id`, `class_id`, `source_type`, `exam_body_id`, `topic_id`, `question`, `difficulty`, `recommended_class`, `term_tag`, `question_category`, `explanation`, `review_status`, `quality_score`, `times_used`, `school_id`, `createdby`, `datecreated`, `dateupdated`, `deleted`, `exam_year`) VALUES
(688, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 16, '<p><small>Source: Geometrical Construction Topic Bank - Item 29</small></p><p><strong>Geometrical Construction - Question 29</strong></p><p>The locus of points equidistant from two parallel lines is</p>', 'Medium', 'JSS3', '', 'Locus', 'A line halfway between two parallel lines is equally distant from both lines.', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 00:24:33', NULL, 0, 0),
(689, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 16, '<p><small>Source: Geometrical Construction Topic Bank - Item 30</small></p><p><strong>Geometrical Construction - Question 30</strong></p><p><img src=\"../uploads/question_bank/geometrical_construction/gc_030.png\" alt=\"Diagram for Geometrical Construction Question 30\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;\"></p><p>In the diagram, the dashed lines are perpendicular bisectors of sides of triangle ABC and meet at O. What is special about point O?</p>', 'Medium', 'JSS3', '', 'Diagram Interpretation', 'The perpendicular bisectors of a triangle meet at the circumcentre, which is equidistant from all three vertices.', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 00:24:33', NULL, 0, 0),
(690, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 16, '<p><small>Source: Geometrical Construction Topic Bank - Item 31</small></p><p><strong>Geometrical Construction - Question 31</strong></p><p>Which information is sufficient to construct a rhombus uniquely?</p>', 'Medium', 'JSS3', '', 'Quadrilaterals', 'A side length and a diagonal determine the positions of the remaining vertices of a rhombus.', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 00:24:33', NULL, 0, 0),
(691, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 16, '<p><small>Source: Geometrical Construction Topic Bank - Item 32</small></p><p><strong>Geometrical Construction - Question 32</strong></p><p>While constructing an angle bisector, a student draws arcs from the two arms using different compass radii. Why is the construction unreliable?</p>', 'Medium', 'JSS3', '', 'Error Detection', 'The arcs drawn from the two arms must have equal radii to locate a point equidistant from both arms.', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 00:24:33', NULL, 0, 0),
(692, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 16, '<p><small>Source: Geometrical Construction Topic Bank - Item 33</small></p><p><strong>Geometrical Construction - Question 33</strong></p><p>How can an angle of 135° be constructed from a straight angle and a perpendicular line?</p>', 'Medium', 'JSS3', '', 'Construction Angles', 'The angle midway between 90° and 180° is (90° + 180°) ÷ 2 = 135°.', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 00:24:33', NULL, 0, 0),
(693, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 16, '<p><small>Source: Geometrical Construction Topic Bank - Item 34</small></p><p><strong>Geometrical Construction - Question 34</strong></p><p><img src=\"../uploads/question_bank/geometrical_construction/gc_034.png\" alt=\"Diagram for Geometrical Construction Question 34\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;\"></p><p>In the diagram, the three dashed lines are angle bisectors of triangle ABC and meet at I. Which statement about I is correct?</p>', 'Medium', 'JSS3', '', 'Diagram Interpretation', 'The angle bisectors of a triangle meet at the incentre, which is equidistant from the three sides.', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 00:24:33', NULL, 0, 0),
(694, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 16, '<p><small>Source: Geometrical Construction Topic Bank - Item 35</small></p><p><strong>Geometrical Construction - Question 35</strong></p><p>A circular fountain is to be placed inside a triangular park so that it is equally distant from the three boundary lines. Which point should be constructed as its centre?</p>', 'Medium', 'JSS3', '', 'Application', 'The angle bisectors meet at the incentre, which is equally distant from all three sides.', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 00:24:34', NULL, 0, 0),
(695, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 16, '<p><small>Source: Geometrical Construction Topic Bank - Item 36</small></p><p><strong>Geometrical Construction - Question 36</strong></p><p><img src=\"../uploads/question_bank/geometrical_construction/gc_036.png\" alt=\"Diagram for Geometrical Construction Question 36\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;\"></p><p>The diagram shows rays forming 60° and 90° at O, with another ray bisecting the angle between them. What angle does the bisecting ray make with OA?</p>', 'Hard', 'JSS3', '', 'Diagram Interpretation', 'The angle halfway between 60° and 90° is (60° + 90°) ÷ 2 = 75°.', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 00:24:34', NULL, 0, 0),
(696, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 16, '<p><small>Source: Geometrical Construction Topic Bank - Item 37</small></p><p><strong>Geometrical Construction - Question 37</strong></p><p>A student attempts to construct a triangle with sides 4 cm, 5 cm and 10 cm. Why will the construction fail?</p>', 'Hard', 'JSS3', '', 'Error Detection', 'For a triangle to exist, the sum of any two sides must be greater than the third side. Here, 4 + 5 < 10.', 'approved', 0, 2, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 00:24:34', NULL, 0, 0),
(697, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 16, '<p><small>Source: Geometrical Construction Topic Bank - Item 38</small></p><p><strong>Geometrical Construction - Question 38</strong></p><p>To construct a tangent to a circle at a point T on its circumference, which line should first be drawn?</p>', 'Hard', 'JSS3', '', 'Circle Construction', 'The radius to the point of contact is drawn first, and the tangent is constructed perpendicular to it at T.', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 00:24:34', NULL, 0, 0),
(698, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 16, '<p><small>Source: Geometrical Construction Topic Bank - Item 39</small></p><p><strong>Geometrical Construction - Question 39</strong></p><p><img src=\"../uploads/question_bank/geometrical_construction/gc_039.png\" alt=\"Diagram for Geometrical Construction Question 39\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;\"></p><p>In the diagram, the dashed line is the perpendicular bisector of AB, while the circle has centre A. Which points satisfy both conditions of being equidistant from A and B and being a fixed distance from A?</p>', 'Hard', 'JSS3', '', 'Locus', 'P and Q lie on both the perpendicular bisector of AB and the circle centred at A.', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 00:24:34', NULL, 0, 0),
(699, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 16, '<p><small>Source: Geometrical Construction Topic Bank - Item 40</small></p><p><strong>Geometrical Construction - Question 40</strong></p><p>When constructing the perpendicular bisector of a line segment AB, a student uses a compass radius shorter than half of AB. What will most likely happen?</p>', 'Hard', 'JSS3', '', 'Error Detection', 'The compass radius must be greater than half the length of AB for the arcs from A and B to intersect above and below the segment.', 'approved', 0, 2, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 00:24:34', NULL, 0, 0),
(700, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 16, '<p><small>Source: Geometrical Construction Topic Bank - Item 41</small></p><p><strong>Geometrical Construction - Question 41</strong></p><p>Triangle ABC is to be constructed with AB = 8 cm, BC = 6 cm and ∠ABC = 70°. Which construction condition is being applied?</p>', 'Hard', 'JSS3', '', 'Triangle Construction', 'Two sides and the included angle are given, so the construction uses SAS.', 'approved', 0, 2, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 00:24:34', NULL, 0, 0),
(701, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 16, '<p><small>Source: Geometrical Construction Topic Bank - Item 42</small></p><p><strong>Geometrical Construction - Question 42</strong></p><p><img src=\"../uploads/question_bank/geometrical_construction/gc_042.png\" alt=\"Diagram for Geometrical Construction Question 42\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;\"></p><p>The diagram shows a circle with centre O and a tangent touching it at T. Which statement is always true?</p>', 'Hard', 'JSS3', '', 'Diagram Interpretation', 'A tangent to a circle is perpendicular to the radius drawn to the point of contact.', 'approved', 0, 2, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 00:24:34', NULL, 0, 0),
(702, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 16, '<p><small>Source: Geometrical Construction Topic Bank - Item 43</small></p><p><strong>Geometrical Construction - Question 43</strong></p><p>Which of the following is the correct first step when constructing the perpendicular bisector of a line segment AB?</p>', 'Hard', 'JSS3', '', 'Construction Procedure', 'The compass opening must be greater than half the length of AB so that the arcs intersect.', 'approved', 0, 2, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 00:24:34', NULL, 0, 0),
(703, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 16, '<p><small>Source: Geometrical Construction Topic Bank - Item 44</small></p><p><strong>Geometrical Construction - Question 44</strong></p><p><img src=\"../uploads/question_bank/geometrical_construction/gc_044.png\" alt=\"Diagram for Geometrical Construction Question 44\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;\"></p><p>In the diagram, point P is equidistant from lines l₁ and l₂. Which construction produced point P?</p>', 'Hard', 'JSS3', '', 'Diagram Interpretation', 'Every point on the angle bisector is equidistant from the two arms of the angle.', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 00:24:34', NULL, 0, 0),
(704, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 16, '<p><small>Source: Geometrical Construction Topic Bank - Item 45</small></p><p><strong>Geometrical Construction - Question 45</strong></p><p>A circle passes through vertices A, B and C of a triangle. The centre of the circle is the</p>', 'Hard', 'JSS3', '', 'Circle Construction', 'The circumcentre is the point where the perpendicular bisectors of the sides meet and is the centre of the circumcircle.', 'approved', 0, 2, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 00:24:34', NULL, 0, 0),
(705, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 16, '<p><small>Source: Geometrical Construction Topic Bank - Item 46</small></p><p><strong>Geometrical Construction - Question 46</strong></p><p><img src=\"../uploads/question_bank/geometrical_construction/gc_046.png\" alt=\"Diagram for Geometrical Construction Question 46\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;\"></p><p>The diagram shows a triangle with a circle touching all three sides internally. The centre of the circle is point I. What is point I called?</p>', 'Hard', 'JSS3', '', 'Diagram Interpretation', 'The centre of the inscribed circle of a triangle is the incentre.', 'approved', 0, 2, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 00:24:34', NULL, 0, 0),
(706, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 16, '<p><small>Source: Geometrical Construction Topic Bank - Item 47</small></p><p><strong>Geometrical Construction - Question 47</strong></p><p>An engineer wants to locate a point that is exactly 5 cm from point A and also exactly 5 cm from point B. Which construction should be used?</p>', 'Hard', 'JSS3', '', 'Application', 'The required point lies at the intersection of two circles having equal radii of 5 cm centred at A and B.', 'approved', 0, 3, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 00:24:34', NULL, 0, 0),
(707, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 16, '<p><small>Source: Geometrical Construction Topic Bank - Item 48</small></p><p><strong>Geometrical Construction - Question 48</strong></p><p>Which sequence of constructions can be used to obtain an angle of 15° accurately?</p>', 'Hard', 'JSS3', '', 'Construction Angles', 'Half of 30° is 15°.', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 00:24:34', NULL, 0, 0),
(708, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 16, '<p><small>Source: Geometrical Construction Topic Bank - Item 49</small></p><p><strong>Geometrical Construction - Question 49</strong></p><p>A student joins the intersection points of two construction arcs with one endpoint of the line segment instead of joining the two arc intersections. What is the result?</p>', 'Hard', 'JSS3', '', 'Error Detection', 'The perpendicular bisector must pass through the two arc intersection points.', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 00:24:34', NULL, 0, 0),
(709, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 16, '<p><small>Source: Geometrical Construction Topic Bank - Item 50</small></p><p><strong>Geometrical Construction - Question 50</strong></p><p>A telecommunications mast is to be erected at a point that is equally distant from three villages represented by the vertices of a triangular map. Which point should be constructed?</p>', 'Hard', 'JSS3', '', 'Application', 'The circumcentre is equidistant from the three vertices of a triangle.', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 00:24:34', NULL, 0, 0),
(710, 18, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Item 1 - Question 1</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Question 1</strong></p><p>Who among the following could be described as the founding father of Nigerian nationalism?</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Nationalism', 'Olayinka Herbert Samuel Macauley (14 November 1864 - 7 May 1946) was a Nigerian nationalist and musician and is\nconsidered by many Nigerians as the founder/father of Nigerian nationalism.', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 09:15:16', NULL, 0, 2025),
(711, 18, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Item 2 - Question 2</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Question 2</strong></p><p>Rule of law means</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Rule of Law', 'Rule of law means supremacy of the law or constitution over and above everybody or citizens. It was propounded by A. V.\nDicey in 1885.', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 09:15:16', NULL, 0, 2025),
(712, 18, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Item 3 - Question 3</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Question 3</strong></p><p>A major characteristic of civil society is</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Civil Society', 'Social responsibility is an ethical framework and suggests that an entity, be it an organization or individual, has an\nobligation to act for the benefit of society at large.', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 09:15:16', NULL, 0, 2025),
(713, 18, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Item 4 - Question 4</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Question 4</strong></p><p><img src=\"../uploads/question_bank/waec_2025_civic_education/Q4_Q5_shared_diagram.png\" alt=\"Diagram for WAEC 2025 Civic Education Questions 4 and 5\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;\"></p><p>Use the diagram above to answer this question\nThe marked pedestrian crossing shown in the diagram is</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Road Safety', 'The marked pedestrian crossing showing is zebra crossing.', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 09:15:16', NULL, 0, 2025),
(714, 18, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Item 5 - Question 5</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Question 5</strong></p><p><img src=\"../uploads/question_bank/waec_2025_civic_education/Q4_Q5_shared_diagram.png\" alt=\"Diagram for WAEC 2025 Civic Education Questions 4 and 5\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;\"></p><p>Use the diagram above to answer this question\nIn the above diagram, all vehicles stopped mainly because</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Road Safety', 'Vehicle stopped mainly because the pedestrians have already stepped on the line as shown in the diagram', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 09:15:16', NULL, 0, 2025),
(715, 18, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Item 6 - Question 6</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Question 6</strong></p><p>Citizenship status is acquired through</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Citizenship', 'Citizenship status can be acquired through several means, including birth, naturalization, honorary and registration.\nBirth refers to being born within a country\'s territory or to its citizens. Naturalization is the process by which a foreign\ncitizen becomes a citizen of another country. Honorary citizenship is granted by a country to a foreign individual in\nrecognition of their contributions or services. Registration can refer to the process of registering as a citizen, often\napplicable to those who have a claim to citizenship through descent.', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 09:15:16', NULL, 0, 2025),
(716, 18, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Item 7 - Question 7</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Question 7</strong></p><p>Human Rights are basic natural rights which people enjoy primarily because they are</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Human Rights', 'Human rights are basic natural right which people enjoy primarily because they are human beings. Human rights are\nrights exercised by human beings.', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 09:15:16', NULL, 0, 2025),
(717, 18, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Item 8 - Question 8</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Question 8</strong></p><p>Interpersonal relationship exists when</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Interpersonal Relationships', 'Interpersonal relationship refers to a strong association among individuals working together in the same organization.\nIndividuals working together are likely to develop interpersonal relationships. One of the most important interpersonal\nrelationships is social interaction in a social setting.', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 09:15:16', NULL, 0, 2025),
(718, 18, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Item 9 - Question 9</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Question 9</strong></p><p>Cultism can be described to be</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Cultism', 'Cultism is a social vice that involves a group of people who share a common belief and are involved in secret practices.\nThese practices are often harmful and dangerous to both members of the cult and non-members. Therefore, cultism can be described as dangerous.', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 09:15:16', NULL, 0, 2025),
(719, 18, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Item 10 - Question 10</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Question 10</strong></p><p>Use the statements below to answer this question</p><p>NEWS: &#039;Rival cult Group Killed Ten on Campus&#039;\nSTUDENT: I will definitely need a bullet proof vest before I can go back to the Campus.</p><p>Based on the statement above, the decision of the student on having a bullet proof vest shows that cultism</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Cultism', 'The decision of the student on having a bullet proof vest shows that cultism spreads or creates fear and terror on the campus', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 09:15:16', NULL, 0, 2025),
(720, 18, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Item 11 - Question 11</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Question 11</strong></p><p>Use the statements below to answer this question</p><p>NEWS: &#039;Rival cult Group Killed Ten on Campus&#039;\nSTUDENT: I will definitely need a bullet proof vest before I can go back to the Campus.</p><p>It could be inferred from the statements above that cultism in schools could lead to</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Cultism', 'The statement \'Rival cult Group Killed Ten on Campus\' implies that cultism in schools can lead to violence and death.\nThe student\'s response further emphasizes the danger, as they feel they would need a bulletproof vest to return to\ncampus. Therefore, the inference that can be drawn from these statements is that cultism in schools could lead to\n\'untimely death\', which is option 4.', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 09:15:16', NULL, 0, 2025),
(721, 18, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Item 12 - Question 12</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Question 12</strong></p><p>Victims of human trafficking are usually compelled to engage in</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Road Safety', 'Victims of human trafficking are usually compelled to engage in forced labour.\nHuman trafficking simply means the trade of humans for the purpose of forced labour, sexual slavery or commercial\nsexual exploitation for the trafficker or others.', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 09:15:16', NULL, 0, 2025),
(722, 18, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Item 13 - Question 13</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Question 13</strong></p><p>One habit which People Living With HIV/AIDS (PLWHAs) must avoid to remain healthy and productive is</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Civic Education', 'People living with HIV/AIDS must avoid to remain healthy and productive, they should avoid self pity or self-\nmedication.', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 09:15:16', NULL, 0, 2025),
(723, 18, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Item 14 - Question 14</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Question 14</strong></p><p>The National Assembly Presidency and Court which are inter-related and interdependent in our democracy constitute the</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Civic Education', 'The National Assembly, Presidency, and Court are the three arms of government in a democratic system. The National\nAssembly (Legislature) makes the laws, the Presidency (Executive) implements the laws, and the Court (Judiciary)\ninterprets the laws. They are inter-related and interdependent, each performing its functions to maintain checks and\nbalances in the system.', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 09:15:16', NULL, 0, 2025),
(724, 18, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Item 15 - Question 15</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Question 15</strong></p><p>A system of government that listens to public opinion and tolerates opposition is</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Civic Education', 'In democratic regime is a system of government that listens to the view or opinion of the people and tolerates\nopposition in the country.', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 09:15:16', NULL, 0, 2025),
(725, 18, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Item 16 - Question 16</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Question 16</strong></p><p>A situation where most citizens fail to vote in elections coud be described as political</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Political Participation', 'Political apathy is a situation where most citizens do not show interest in politics or fails to vote during the elections.', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 09:15:16', NULL, 0, 2025),
(726, 18, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Item 17 - Question 17</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Question 17</strong></p><p>The division of Nigeria into various constituencies with each electing a person to represent it in the National Assemblyis a demonstration of</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Civic Education', 'The division of Nigeria into various constituencies with each electing a person to represent it in the National assembly is\na demonstration of popular participation.', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 09:15:16', NULL, 0, 2025),
(727, 18, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Item 18 - Question 18</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Question 18</strong></p><p>In Nigeria, public servants are expected to be</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Political Participation', 'In Nigeria, public servants are expected to be non-partisan. This means they should not show support for any political\nparty or be involved in political activities. This is to ensure that they serve all citizens equally without any bias or\nfavoritism. Being non-partisan is a key principle of public service, not just in Nigeria, but in many countries around the\nworld.', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 09:15:16', NULL, 0, 2025),
(728, 18, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Item 19 - Question 19</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Question 19</strong></p><p>The principle that public servants cannot be held responsible for their official actions denotes</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Civic Education', 'Anonymity is a principle that states that public servants can not be held responsible for their official actions.', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 09:15:16', NULL, 0, 2025),
(729, 18, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Item 20 - Question 20</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Question 20</strong></p><p>Universal Declaration of Human Rights (UDHR) is based on the resolution of the</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Human Rights', 'Universal Declaration of Human Rights is based on the resolution of the United Nations Organisation (UNO).', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 09:15:16', NULL, 0, 2025),
(730, 18, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Item 21 - Question 21</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Question 21</strong></p><p>Use the story below to answer this questionImoh lived with her parents in Kakuri. They were good citizens who detested all forms of immoral acts. Both at homeand in school, Imoh had been taught the virtues and values of a good citizen. However, while in a bus on her way homefrom school, the conductor forgot to ask her fare. She knew that the right thing to do was to pay even when theconductor had forgotten to collect the fare. She also knew that there were other things she could do with the money ifit was not paid, but she did what was expected by informing the conductor and paying the fare.According to the story, Imoh&#039;s parents were</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Civic Education', 'From the story, it is clear that Imoh\'s parents have instilled in her the values of honesty and responsibility. They are\ndescribed as good citizens who detest all forms of immoral acts. This suggests that they are honest and responsible\nindividuals, not necessarily wealthy, prominent politicians, or religious fanatics.', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 09:15:16', NULL, 0, 2025),
(731, 18, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Item 22 - Question 22</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Question 22</strong></p><p>Use the story below to answer this questionImoh lived with her parents in Kakuri. They were good citizens who detested all forms of immoral acts. Both at homeand in school, Imoh had been taught the virtues and values of a good citizen. However, while in a bus on her way homefrom school, the conductor forgot to ask her fare. She knew that the right thing to do was to pay even when theconductor had forgotten to collect the fare. She also knew that there were other things she could do with the money ifit was not paid, but she did what was expected by informing the conductor and paying the fare.What value did Imoh demonstrate?</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Civic Education', 'Imoh demonstrated honesty. honesty is a virtue that involves being truthful and sincere. in the story, imh was transparent by informing the conductor about the unpaid fare and paying it, even though the conductor had forgotten to collect it.', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 09:15:16', NULL, 0, 2025),
(732, 18, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Item 23 - Question 23</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Question 23</strong></p><p>Conflicts are better resolved in the society through</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Civic Education', 'Conflicts are better resolved in the society through dialogue. Dialogue is a method of conflict resolution that involves\nopen, honest, and respectful communication between parties involved in a conflict. It allows for understanding,\ncompromise, and peaceful resolution of conflicts. While tribunal, litigation, and court are also methods of conflict\nresolution, they are often more adversarial and may not lead to the best resolution for all parties involved.', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 09:15:16', NULL, 0, 2025),
(733, 18, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Item 24 - Question 24</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Question 24</strong></p><p>To prevent the spread of HIV/AIDS, people should be encouraged to</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Civic Education', 'HIV/AIDS is primarily spread through unprotected sexual intercourse with an infected person. Therefore, avoiding casual\nsexual activities can significantly reduce the risk of contracting or spreading the virus. This does not necessarily mean\nthat people should marry early in life, engage in gainful employment, or pursue higher education. These options may\nhave other benefits, but they do not directly prevent the spread of HIV/AIDS.', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 09:15:16', NULL, 0, 2025),
(734, 18, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Item 25 - Question 25</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Question 25</strong></p><p>The nearest government to the people and an important means of promoting grassroots development is the</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Civic Education', 'Local government is the nearest government that is close to the grass root people and promote government at grass root', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 09:15:16', NULL, 0, 2025),
(735, 18, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Item 26 - Question 26</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Question 26</strong></p><p>Democratic governance is usually characterized by</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Political Participation', 'Democratic governance is characterized by free, fair, and credible elections. This is because democracy is a system of\ngovernment where citizens exercise power by voting. In a democratic system, the citizens have the right to vote in order\nto choose their representatives in the government. The process of voting should be free, fair, and credible to ensure that\nthe will of the people is accurately represented.', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 09:15:16', NULL, 0, 2025),
(736, 18, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Item 27 - Question 27</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Question 27</strong></p><p>Political apathy often leads to</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Political Participation', 'Political apathy is when the citizens of a country are not interested or involved in politics and this lead to low level of\nparticipation.', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 09:15:16', NULL, 0, 2025),
(737, 18, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Item 28 - Question 28</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Question 28</strong></p><p>Which of the following is not necessary for public servants to perform effectively?</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Civic Education', 'The effectiveness of public servants is not directly influenced by the acceptance of foreign aid by the government. Public\nservants\' performance is more related to their skills, training, resources, and the institutional framework within which\nthey operate. Acceptance of foreign aid by the government is a policy decision that may indirectly affect public service\nby providing additional resources or imposing certain conditions, but it is not a necessary condition for publie servants\nto perform effectively.', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 09:15:16', NULL, 0, 2025),
(738, 18, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Item 29 - Question 29</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Question 29</strong></p><p>One of the conditions which can limit the enjoyment of Human Rights in Nigeria is the</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Human Rights', 'The declaration of a state of emergency by the government can limit the enjoyment of human rights. During a state of\nemergency, certain civil liberties can be suspended, such as freedom of assembly, freedom of movement, and the right to\na fair trial. This is done to maintain order and security during a crisis. Therefore, the declaration of a state of emergency\nis a condition that can limit the enjoyment of human rights in Nigeria.', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 09:15:16', NULL, 0, 2025),
(739, 18, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Item 30 - Question 30</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Question 30</strong></p><p><img src=\"../uploads/question_bank/waec_2025_civic_education/Q30_Q31_shared_diagram.png\" alt=\"Diagram for WAEC 2025 Civic Education Questions 30 and 31\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;\"></p><p>The drunkard as depicted in the picture will not likely perform his parental role because</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Responsible Parenthood', 'The drunkard as depicted in the picture will not likely perform his parental role because his action constitutes bad\ninfluence', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 09:15:16', NULL, 0, 2025),
(740, 18, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Item 31 - Question 31</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Question 31</strong></p><p><img src=\"../uploads/question_bank/waec_2025_civic_education/Q30_Q31_shared_diagram.png\" alt=\"Diagram for WAEC 2025 Civic Education Questions 30 and 31\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;\"></p><p>The above picture portrays drunkenness mainly as</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Responsible Parenthood', 'The picture portrays drunkenness mainly as an environmental nuisance.', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 09:15:16', NULL, 0, 2025),
(741, 18, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Item 32 - Question 32</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Question 32</strong></p><p>The implication of positive communal relationships is that it</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Communal Relationships', 'Positive communal relationships promotes solidarity and love. It also promote diplomatic relationships among the\npeople.', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 09:15:16', NULL, 0, 2025),
(742, 18, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Item 33 - Question 33</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Question 33</strong></p><p>One major factor that attracts some Nigerians into human trafficking is</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Road Safety', 'The major factor that attracts some Nigerians into human trafficking is insatiable quest for quick wealth.', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 09:15:16', NULL, 0, 2025),
(743, 18, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Item 34 - Question 34</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Question 34</strong></p><p>One of the reasons most HIV/AIDS patients are reluctant to disclose their status is because of</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Civic Education', 'Fear of social stigmatization is one of the reasons most HIV/AIDS patients are reluctant to disclose their status.', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 09:15:16', NULL, 0, 2025),
(744, 18, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Item 35 - Question 35</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Question 35</strong></p><p>Use the report below to answer this question.The Bawali High Court has ordered the police in Area Z Command to produce Mr. Zeb, who is in police custody for analleged offence. The court insists that Mr. Zeb cannot be punished until he is found guilty of breach of any law of theland by a court of competent jurisdiction.The position of the court on this matter justifies the essence of the</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Rule of Law', 'The position of the Court on this matter justifies the essence of the rule of law. A person or an accused person is\npresume innocent until it is found guilty by the court of law.', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 09:15:16', NULL, 0, 2025),
(745, 18, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Item 36 - Question 36</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Question 36</strong></p><p>Leaders can best protect the interest of their followers by</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Civic Education', 'Creating Conducive atmosphere for participation is one of the way a leader can protect the interest of their followers.', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 09:15:16', NULL, 0, 2025),
(746, 18, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Item 37 - Question 37</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Question 37</strong></p><p>Civil societies are vital for the promotion of popular participation because they are</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Political Participation', 'Civil societies are non-profit organizations that are involved in promoting political education among the citizens. They\nare not profit-oriented organizations, they are not necessarily engaged in developmental programmes, and they are not\nformidable oppositions to government. They are involved in political education because they help to educate the citizens\nabout their rights, responsibilities, and the workings of the government. This helps to promote popular participation in\nthe political process as more informed citizens are more likely to participate actively in the political process.', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 09:15:16', NULL, 0, 2025),
(747, 18, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Item 38 - Question 38</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Question 38</strong></p><p>Use the dialogue below to answer this question.</p><p>Ada: Wanja, where are you going to in this ungodly hour of the night?\nWanja: I am heading towards my usual joint to enjoy myself.\nAda: Which joint?\nWanja: XYZ Night Club, where I take marijuana and alcoholic beverages. I really want to be high tonight so that when people see me tomorrow, they will fear and respect me.\nAda: Remember, people who work under the influence of hard drugs and alcoholic beverages are prone to either psychiatric problems or premature death.\nAda: Softly young man, imbibe good-natured character, you have the world at your feet and a destiny to fulfill. Pray you will not be the architect of your own misfortune.From this dialogue, it is very likely that Wanja will be exhibiting the following characters except</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Drug Abuse', 'From this dialogue, it is very likely that Wanja will not exhibit the character of hospitable attitude towards people.', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 09:15:16', NULL, 0, 2025),
(748, 18, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Item 39 - Question 39</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Question 39</strong></p><p>Use the dialogue below to answer this question.</p><p>Ada: Wanja, where are you going to in this ungodly hour of the night?\nWanja: I am heading towards my usual joint to enjoy myself.\nAda: Which joint?\nWanja: XYZ Night Club, where I take marijuana and alcoholic beverages. I really want to be high tonight so that when people see me tomorrow, they will fear and respect me.\nAda: Remember, people who work under the influence of hard drugs and alcoholic beverages are prone to either psychiatric problems or premature death.\nAda: Softly young man, imbibe good-natured character, you have the world at your feet and a destiny to fulfill. Pray you will not be the architect of your own misfortune.Which of the following may result from Wanja&#039;s habit?</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Drug Abuse', 'Criminality in the society may result from Wanja\'s habit smoking and alcohols result in bad friendstand this lead to\ncriminality in the society.', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 09:15:16', NULL, 0, 2025),
(749, 18, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Item 40 - Question 40</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Question 40</strong></p><p>Use the dialogue below to answer this question.</p><p>Ada: Wanja, where are you going to in this ungodly hour of the night?\nWanja: I am heading towards my usual joint to enjoy myself.\nAda: Which joint?\nWanja: XYZ Night Club, where I take marijuana and alcoholic beverages. I really want to be high tonight so that when people see me tomorrow, they will fear and respect me.\nAda: Remember, people who work under the influence of hard drugs and alcoholic beverages are prone to either psychiatric problems or premature death.\nAda: Softly young man, imbibe good-natured character, you have the world at your feet and a destiny to fulfill. Pray you will not be the architect of your own misfortune.From Ada&#039;s admonition, it could be deduced that taking hard drugs could</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Drug Abuse', 'From Ada\'s admonition, it could be deduced that taking hard drugs could lead to insanity of thetaddictss', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 09:15:16', NULL, 0, 2025),
(750, 18, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Item 41 - Question 41</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Question 41</strong></p><p>Use the dialogue below to answer this question.</p><p>Ada: Wanja, where are you going to in this ungodly hour of the night?\nWanja: I am heading towards my usual joint to enjoy myself.\nAda: Which joint?\nWanja: XYZ Night Club, where I take marijuana and alcoholic beverages. I really want to be high tonight so that when people see me tomorrow, they will fear and respect me.\nAda: Remember, people who work under the influence of hard drugs and alcoholic beverages are prone to either psychiatric problems or premature death.\nAda: Softly young man, imbibe good-natured character, you have the world at your feet and a destiny to fulfill. Pray you will not be the architect of your own misfortune.From the above dialogue, Wanja&#039;s behavior could be curtailed by</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Drug Abuse', 'From the dialogue, Wanja is involved in substance abuse and this behavior can be curtailed through re-orientation and\nrehabilitation. Re-orientation involves changing his perspective about substance abuse and its effects, while\nrehabilitation involves helping him overcome his addiction. Sending him abroad for further studies or indulging him\nwith expensive gifts may not necessarily change his behavior. Financial inducement may even worsen the situation as\nhe may use the money to buy more drugs.', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 09:15:16', NULL, 0, 2025),
(751, 18, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Item 42 - Question 42</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Question 42</strong></p><p>Use the dialogue below to answer this question.</p><p>Ada: Wanja, where are you going to in this ungodly hour of the night?\nWanja: I am heading towards my usual joint to enjoy myself.\nAda: Which joint?\nWanja: XYZ Night Club, where I take marijuana and alcoholic beverages. I really want to be high tonight so that when people see me tomorrow, they will fear and respect me.\nAda: Remember, people who work under the influence of hard drugs and alcoholic beverages are prone to either psychiatric problems or premature death.\nAda: Softly young man, imbibe good-natured character, you have the world at your feet and a destiny to fulfill. Pray you will not be the architect of your own misfortune.Which of the following governmental agencies is the most capable of controlling the activities of Wanja and his group?</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Drug Abuse', 'National Drug Law Enforcement Agency (NDLEA) is governmental agencies that is capable of controlling the activities\nof Wanja and his group. NDLEA are charge with the responsibility of orientate the drug addicts.to', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 09:15:16', NULL, 0, 2025),
(752, 18, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Item 43 - Question 43</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Question 43</strong></p><p>Use the dialogue below to answer this question.</p><p>Ada: Wanja, where are you going to in this ungodly hour of the night?\nWanja: I am heading towards my usual joint to enjoy myself.\nAda: Which joint?\nWanja: XYZ Night Club, where I take marijuana and alcoholic beverages. I really want to be high tonight so that when people see me tomorrow, they will fear and respect me.\nAda: Remember, people who work under the influence of hard drugs and alcoholic beverages are prone to either psychiatric problems or premature death.\nAda: Softly young man, imbibe good-natured character, you have the world at your feet and a destiny to fulfill. Pray you will not be the architect of your own misfortune.One of the major barriers to national development is the</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Drug Abuse', 'The dialogue suggests that drug and alcohol abuse, which can be seen as a form of social corruptiontis a major barrier\nto national development.', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 09:15:17', NULL, 0, 2025),
(753, 18, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Item 44 - Question 44</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Question 44</strong></p><p>Use the dialogue below to answer this question.</p><p>Ada: Wanja, where are you going to in this ungodly hour of the night?\nWanja: I am heading towards my usual joint to enjoy myself.\nAda: Which joint?\nWanja: XYZ Night Club, where I take marijuana and alcoholic beverages. I really want to be high tonight so that when people see me tomorrow, they will fear and respect me.\nAda: Remember, people who work under the influence of hard drugs and alcoholic beverages are prone to either psychiatric problems or premature death.\nAda: Softly young man, imbibe good-natured character, you have the world at your feet and a destiny to fulfill. Pray you will not be the architect of your own misfortune.The quotation above shows that the speaker is concerned about</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Drug Abuse', 'The dialogue shows that Ada is concerned about Wanja\'s welfare, which is why she warns him about the dangers of\ndrug and alcohol abuse and advises him to lead a good life.', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 09:15:17', NULL, 0, 2025),
(754, 18, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Item 45 - Question 45</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Question 45</strong></p><p>A major benefit of youth empowerment is</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Youth Empowerment', 'Reduction in crime rate is a major benefit of Youth empowerment. It is believed that when youths are engaged the crime\nrate reduced.', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 09:15:17', NULL, 0, 2025),
(755, 18, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Item 46 - Question 46</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Question 46</strong></p><p>Use the story below to answer this question.</p><p>Chief Bilisi was prominent politician and honourable minister in Kantogo Republic. He had sponsored several candidates to power and made them to swear oath of allegiance to him. In return, they awarded contracts and offered financial and material assistance to him at the expense of the public. This had resulted in the non-provision of social amenities. These were some of the grievances the community had against him for which a mob gathered in front of his house shouting and hurling abusive words at him. They did not stop at that as they vandalized property and obstructedvehicular movement.</p><p>When leaders like Chief Bilisi place self interest above public goods, the result is that</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Communal Relationships', 'When leaders like Chief Bilisi place self interest above public goods, the result is that rebellion becomes inevitable.', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 09:15:17', NULL, 0, 2025),
(756, 18, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Item 47 - Question 47</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Question 47</strong></p><p>Use the story below to answer this question.</p><p>Chief Bilisi was prominent politician and honourable minister in Kantogo Republic. He had sponsored several candidates to power and made them to swear oath of allegiance to him. In return, they awarded contracts and offered financial and material assistance to him at the expense of the public. This had resulted in the non-provision of social amenities. These were some of the grievances the community had against him for which a mob gathered in front of his house shouting and hurling abusive words at him. They did not stop at that as they vandalized property and obstructedvehicular movement.</p><p>The condition of disorderly behaviour exhibited by the mob in the story best describes the</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Communal Relationships', 'The condition of disorderly behaviour exhibited by the mob in the story best describes the breakdown of law and\norder in the society or country.', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 09:15:17', NULL, 0, 2025),
(757, 18, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Item 48 - Question 48</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Question 48</strong></p><p>Use the story below to answer this question.</p><p>Chief Bilisi was prominent politician and honourable minister in Kantogo Republic. He had sponsored several candidates to power and made them to swear oath of allegiance to him. In return, they awarded contracts and offered financial and material assistance to him at the expense of the public. This had resulted in the non-provision of social amenities. These were some of the grievances the community had against him for which a mob gathered in front of his house shouting and hurling abusive words at him. They did not stop at that as they vandalized property and obstructedvehicular movement.</p><p>A major lesson Nigerians could learn from the story is that</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Communal Relationships', 'A major lesson Nigerians could learn from the story is that greed and related vices can cause serious breach of the law', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 09:15:17', NULL, 0, 2025);
INSERT INTO `question_bank` (`id`, `subject_id`, `class_id`, `source_type`, `exam_body_id`, `topic_id`, `question`, `difficulty`, `recommended_class`, `term_tag`, `question_category`, `explanation`, `review_status`, `quality_score`, `times_used`, `school_id`, `createdby`, `datecreated`, `dateupdated`, `deleted`, `exam_year`) VALUES
(758, 18, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Item 49 - Question 49</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Question 49</strong></p><p>Youth empowerment is best described as the</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Youth Empowerment', 'Youth empowerment is described as the training given individuals for acquiring means of livelihood to earn a living.', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 09:15:17', NULL, 0, 2025),
(759, 18, 0, 'exam_body', 1, 0, '<p><small>Source: WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Item 50 - Question 50</small></p><p><strong>WAEC 2025 Civic Education - Question 50</strong></p><p>The most popular means through which citizens of a country can participate in politics is by</p>', 'Medium', 'SSS3', '', 'Political Participation', 'Voting in elections is one of the ways a citizen of a country participate in politics. Citizens participate in politics by\nexercising his franchise right.\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 09:15:17', NULL, 0, 2025),
(760, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 17, '<p><small>Source: Measures of Central Tendency and Range Topic Bank - Item 1</small></p><p><strong>Measures of Central Tendency and Range - Question 1</strong></p><p>Find the mean of 4, 6, 8, 10 and 12.</p>', 'Easy', 'JSS2/JSS3', '', 'Mean', '(4 + 6 + 8 + 10 + 12) ÷ 5 = 40 ÷ 5 = 8.', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 10:32:10', NULL, 0, 0),
(761, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 17, '<p><small>Source: Measures of Central Tendency and Range Topic Bank - Item 2</small></p><p><strong>Measures of Central Tendency and Range - Question 2</strong></p><p>Find the median of 5, 7, 9, 11 and 13.</p>', 'Easy', 'JSS2/JSS3', '', 'Median', 'The middle value of the ordered data is 9.', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 10:32:10', NULL, 0, 0),
(762, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 17, '<p><small>Source: Measures of Central Tendency and Range Topic Bank - Item 3</small></p><p><strong>Measures of Central Tendency and Range - Question 3</strong></p><p>Find the mode of 3, 5, 5, 7, 8.</p>', 'Easy', 'JSS2/JSS3', '', 'Mode', '5 occurs more often than any other value.', 'approved', 0, 2, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 10:32:10', NULL, 0, 0),
(763, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 17, '<p><small>Source: Measures of Central Tendency and Range Topic Bank - Item 4</small></p><p><strong>Measures of Central Tendency and Range - Question 4</strong></p><p>Find the range of 8, 10, 12, 15 and 18.</p>', 'Easy', 'JSS2/JSS3', '', 'Range', 'Range = 18 − 8 = 10.', 'approved', 0, 2, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 10:32:10', NULL, 0, 0),
(764, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 17, '<p><small>Source: Measures of Central Tendency and Range Topic Bank - Item 5</small></p><p><strong>Measures of Central Tendency and Range - Question 5</strong></p><p>The marks scored by a student are 15, 18, 20, 22 and 25. Find the mean mark.</p>', 'Easy', 'JSS2/JSS3', '', 'Mean', '(15 + 18 + 20 + 22 + 25) ÷ 5 = 100 ÷ 5 = 20.', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 10:32:10', NULL, 0, 0),
(765, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 17, '<p><small>Source: Measures of Central Tendency and Range Topic Bank - Item 6</small></p><p><strong>Measures of Central Tendency and Range - Question 6</strong></p><p>Find the median of 2, 4, 6, 8, 10, 12.</p>', 'Easy', 'JSS2/JSS3', '', 'Median', 'Median = (6 + 8) ÷ 2 = 7.', 'approved', 0, 2, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 10:32:10', NULL, 0, 0),
(766, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 17, '<p><small>Source: Measures of Central Tendency and Range Topic Bank - Item 7</small></p><p><strong>Measures of Central Tendency and Range - Question 7</strong></p><p>What is the mode of 9, 8, 7, 9, 6, 5, 9?</p>', 'Easy', 'JSS2/JSS3', '', 'Mode', '9 appears three times, more than any other value.', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 10:32:10', NULL, 0, 0),
(767, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 17, '<p><small>Source: Measures of Central Tendency and Range Topic Bank - Item 8</small></p><p><strong>Measures of Central Tendency and Range - Question 8</strong></p><p>Find the range of the data: 14, 17, 19, 20, 22.</p>', 'Easy', 'JSS2/JSS3', '', 'Range', 'Range = 22 − 14 = 8.', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 10:32:10', NULL, 0, 0),
(768, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 17, '<p><small>Source: Measures of Central Tendency and Range Topic Bank - Item 9</small></p><p><strong>Measures of Central Tendency and Range - Question 9</strong></p><p>Which measure of central tendency is the value that occurs most frequently in a data set?</p>', 'Easy', 'JSS2/JSS3', '', 'Mixed Measures', 'The mode is the value with the highest frequency.', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 10:32:10', NULL, 0, 0),
(769, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 17, '<p><small>Source: Measures of Central Tendency and Range Topic Bank - Item 10</small></p><p><strong>Measures of Central Tendency and Range - Question 10</strong></p><p>Which measure is obtained by subtracting the smallest value from the largest value in a data set?</p>', 'Easy', 'JSS2/JSS3', '', 'Mixed Measures', 'Range = Largest value − Smallest value.', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 10:32:10', NULL, 0, 0),
(770, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 17, '<p><small>Source: Measures of Central Tendency and Range Topic Bank - Item 11</small></p><p><strong>Measures of Central Tendency and Range - Question 11</strong></p><p>The mean of the numbers 12, 15, 18, 21 and x is 18. Find the value of x.</p>', 'Medium', 'JSS2/JSS3', '', 'Mean', 'Total = 18 × 5 = 90. Sum of known numbers = 66. Therefore, x = 90 − 66 = 24.', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 10:32:10', NULL, 0, 0),
(771, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 17, '<p><small>Source: Measures of Central Tendency and Range Topic Bank - Item 12</small></p><p><strong>Measures of Central Tendency and Range - Question 12</strong></p><p>The average score of 8 students is 14. What is the total of their scores?</p>', 'Medium', 'JSS2/JSS3', '', 'Mean', 'Total score = Mean × Number of students = 14 × 8 = 112.', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 10:32:10', NULL, 0, 0),
(772, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 17, '<p><small>Source: Measures of Central Tendency and Range Topic Bank - Item 13</small></p><p><strong>Measures of Central Tendency and Range - Question 13</strong></p><p>Find the median of 16, 12, 18, 20, 14, 22 and 24.</p>', 'Medium', 'JSS2/JSS3', '', 'Median', 'Ordered data: 12, 14, 16, 18, 20, 22, 24. The middle value is 18.', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 10:32:10', NULL, 0, 0),
(773, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 17, '<p><small>Source: Measures of Central Tendency and Range Topic Bank - Item 14</small></p><p><strong>Measures of Central Tendency and Range - Question 14</strong></p><p>A student found the median of 11, 7, 15, 13 and 9 as 15. Why is the answer incorrect?</p>', 'Medium', 'JSS2/JSS3', '', 'Error Detection', 'The data should first be arranged: 7, 9, 11, 13, 15. The median is 11.', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 10:32:10', NULL, 0, 0),
(774, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 17, '<p><small>Source: Measures of Central Tendency and Range Topic Bank - Item 15</small></p><p><strong>Measures of Central Tendency and Range - Question 15</strong></p><p>The shoe sizes of 10 students are 38, 39, 40, 39, 41, 39, 40, 42, 40, 39. What is the mode?</p>', 'Medium', 'JSS2/JSS3', '', 'Mode', '39 appears four times, more than any other value.', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 10:32:10', NULL, 0, 0),
(775, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 17, '<p><small>Source: Measures of Central Tendency and Range Topic Bank - Item 16</small></p><p><strong>Measures of Central Tendency and Range - Question 16</strong></p><p>The temperatures recorded over five days were 28°C, 31°C, 30°C, 35°C and 29°C. Find the range.</p>', 'Medium', 'JSS2/JSS3', '', 'Range', 'Range = 35 − 28 = 7°C.', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 10:32:10', NULL, 0, 0),
(776, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 17, '<p><small>Source: Measures of Central Tendency and Range Topic Bank - Item 17</small></p><p><strong>Measures of Central Tendency and Range - Question 17</strong></p><p>The table shows the scores of students. Score: 2 3 4 5 Frequency: 1 3 4 2 What is the mode?</p>', 'Medium', 'JSS2/JSS3', '', 'Frequency Table', 'The highest frequency is 4, corresponding to a score of 4.', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 10:32:10', NULL, 0, 0),
(777, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 17, '<p><small>Source: Measures of Central Tendency and Range Topic Bank - Item 18</small></p><p><strong>Measures of Central Tendency and Range - Question 18</strong></p><p>The table shows the number of books read by students. Books: 1 2 3 4 Frequency: 2 5 3 2 How many students were surveyed?</p>', 'Medium', 'JSS2/JSS3', '', 'Frequency Table', 'Total students = 2 + 5 + 3 + 2 = 12.', 'approved', 0, 2, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 10:32:10', NULL, 0, 0),
(778, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 17, '<p><small>Source: Measures of Central Tendency and Range Topic Bank - Item 19</small></p><p><strong>Measures of Central Tendency and Range - Question 19</strong></p><p>Five friends shared ₦2,500 equally. What was the mean amount received by each friend?</p>', 'Medium', 'JSS2/JSS3', '', 'Word Problem', '₦2,500 ÷ 5 = ₦500.', 'approved', 0, 2, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 10:32:10', NULL, 0, 0),
(779, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 17, '<p><small>Source: Measures of Central Tendency and Range Topic Bank - Item 20</small></p><p><strong>Measures of Central Tendency and Range - Question 20</strong></p><p>The data set is 6, 8, 8, 9, 10, 11 and 14. Which statement is correct?</p>', 'Medium', 'JSS2/JSS3', '', 'Mixed Measures', 'Median = 9. Mode = 8. Range = 14 - 6 = 8. Mean = 66 ÷ 7 ≈ 9.43. The mode and range are both 8, so option C is correct.', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 10:32:10', NULL, 0, 0),
(780, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 17, '<p><small>Source: Measures of Central Tendency and Range Topic Bank - Item 21</small></p><p><strong>Measures of Central Tendency and Range - Question 21</strong></p><p>The mean age of 6 students is 15 years. If five of the students are 14, 15, 16, 15 and 13 years old, what is the age of the sixth student?</p>', 'Medium', 'JSS2/JSS3', '', 'Mean', 'Total age = 15 × 6 = 90. Sum of known ages = 73. Sixth age = 90 − 73 = 17 years.', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 10:32:10', NULL, 0, 0),
(781, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 17, '<p><small>Source: Measures of Central Tendency and Range Topic Bank - Item 22</small></p><p><strong>Measures of Central Tendency and Range - Question 22</strong></p><p>The mean of five numbers is 24. If another number, 30, is added to the data set, what is the new mean?</p>', 'Medium', 'JSS2/JSS3', '', 'Mean', 'Original total = 24 × 5 = 120. New total = 120 + 30 = 150. New mean = 150 ÷ 6 = 25.', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 10:32:10', NULL, 0, 0),
(782, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 17, '<p><small>Source: Measures of Central Tendency and Range Topic Bank - Item 23</small></p><p><strong>Measures of Central Tendency and Range - Question 23</strong></p><p>Find the median of the data set: 21, 15, 17, 19, 13, 25, 23.</p>', 'Medium', 'JSS2/JSS3', '', 'Median', 'Ordered data: 13, 15, 17, 19, 21, 23, 25. The middle value is 19.', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 10:32:10', NULL, 0, 0),
(783, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 17, '<p><small>Source: Measures of Central Tendency and Range Topic Bank - Item 24</small></p><p><strong>Measures of Central Tendency and Range - Question 24</strong></p><p>Find the mode of the data: 12, 10, 9, 12, 8, 10, 12, 9.</p>', 'Medium', 'JSS2/JSS3', '', 'Mode', '12 appears three times, more than any other value.', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 10:32:10', NULL, 0, 0),
(784, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 17, '<p><small>Source: Measures of Central Tendency and Range Topic Bank - Item 25</small></p><p><strong>Measures of Central Tendency and Range - Question 25</strong></p><p>The heights (in cm) of five students are 145, 148, 152, 150 and 147. Find the range.</p>', 'Medium', 'JSS2/JSS3', '', 'Range', 'Range = 152 − 145 = 7 cm.', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 10:32:10', NULL, 0, 0),
(785, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 17, '<p><small>Source: Measures of Central Tendency and Range Topic Bank - Item 26</small></p><p><strong>Measures of Central Tendency and Range - Question 26</strong></p><p>The table shows the number of goals scored by a football team. Goals: 0 1 2 3 Frequency: 2 5 4 1 What is the total number of matches played?</p>', 'Medium', 'JSS2/JSS3', '', 'Frequency Table', 'Total matches = 2 + 5 + 4 + 1 = 12.', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 10:32:10', NULL, 0, 0),
(786, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 17, '<p><small>Source: Measures of Central Tendency and Range Topic Bank - Item 27</small></p><p><strong>Measures of Central Tendency and Range - Question 27</strong></p><p>The table below shows the scores obtained by students. Score: 5 6 7 8 Frequency: 3 4 5 2 Which score is the mode?</p>', 'Medium', 'JSS2/JSS3', '', 'Frequency Table', 'The highest frequency is 5, corresponding to the score 7.', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 10:32:10', NULL, 0, 0),
(787, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 17, '<p><small>Source: Measures of Central Tendency and Range Topic Bank - Item 28</small></p><p><strong>Measures of Central Tendency and Range - Question 28</strong></p><p>A trader sold 20, 25, 30, 35 and 40 bags of rice on five market days. What was the average number of bags sold per day?</p>', 'Medium', 'JSS2/JSS3', '', 'Word Problem', '(20 + 25 + 30 + 35 + 40) ÷ 5 = 150 ÷ 5 = 30.', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 10:32:10', NULL, 0, 0),
(788, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 17, '<p><small>Source: Measures of Central Tendency and Range Topic Bank - Item 29</small></p><p><strong>Measures of Central Tendency and Range - Question 29</strong></p><p>The scores of five students are 45, 45, 50, 55 and 80. Which measure of central tendency is most affected by the unusually high score of 80?</p>', 'Medium', 'JSS2/JSS3', '', 'Data Interpretation', 'The mean is affected more by extreme values than the median or mode.', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 10:32:10', NULL, 0, 0),
(789, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 17, '<p><small>Source: Measures of Central Tendency and Range Topic Bank - Item 30</small></p><p><strong>Measures of Central Tendency and Range - Question 30</strong></p><p>A student calculated the range of 18, 25, 20, 27 and 21 as 27 − 20 = 7. What mistake did the student make?</p>', 'Medium', 'JSS2/JSS3', '', 'Error Detection', 'Range = Largest − Smallest = 27 − 18 = 9, not 27 − 20.', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 10:32:10', NULL, 0, 0),
(790, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 17, '<p><small>Source: Measures of Central Tendency and Range Topic Bank - Item 31</small></p><p><strong>Measures of Central Tendency and Range - Question 31</strong></p><p>The mean of 7, 9, 12, 14 and x is 11. Find x.</p>', 'Medium', 'JSS2/JSS3', '', 'Mean', 'Total = 11 × 5 = 55. Sum of known values = 42. Therefore, x = 55 − 42 = 13.', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 10:32:10', NULL, 0, 0),
(791, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 17, '<p><small>Source: Measures of Central Tendency and Range Topic Bank - Item 32</small></p><p><strong>Measures of Central Tendency and Range - Question 32</strong></p><p>The table shows the scores of some students. Score: 2 4 6 8 Frequency: 3 2 4 1 Find the mean score.</p>', 'Medium', 'JSS2/JSS3', '', 'Frequency Table', 'Total score = 2×3 + 4×2 + 6×4 + 8×1 = 46. Total frequency = 10. Mean = 46 ÷ 10 = 4.6.', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 10:32:10', NULL, 0, 0),
(792, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 17, '<p><small>Source: Measures of Central Tendency and Range Topic Bank - Item 33</small></p><p><strong>Measures of Central Tendency and Range - Question 33</strong></p><p>Find the median of 18, 12, 20, 16, 14 and 22.</p>', 'Medium', 'JSS2/JSS3', '', 'Median', 'Ordered data: 12, 14, 16, 18, 20, 22. Median = (16 + 18) ÷ 2 = 17.', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 10:32:10', NULL, 0, 0),
(793, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 17, '<p><small>Source: Measures of Central Tendency and Range Topic Bank - Item 34</small></p><p><strong>Measures of Central Tendency and Range - Question 34</strong></p><p>The marks obtained by students are 6, 7, 8, 7, 9, 8, 10 and 11. Which statement is correct?</p>', 'Medium', 'JSS2/JSS3', '', 'Mode', 'Both 7 and 8 occur twice, more than any other value. Therefore, the data is bimodal.', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 10:32:10', NULL, 0, 0),
(794, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 17, '<p><small>Source: Measures of Central Tendency and Range Topic Bank - Item 35</small></p><p><strong>Measures of Central Tendency and Range - Question 35</strong></p><p>The range of the data 9, 12, 15, 18 and x is 14. If x is the largest value, find x.</p>', 'Medium', 'JSS2/JSS3', '', 'Range', 'Range = Largest − Smallest. Since the smallest value is 9, x − 9 = 14. Therefore, x = 23.', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 10:32:10', NULL, 0, 0),
(795, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 17, '<p><small>Source: Measures of Central Tendency and Range Topic Bank - Item 36</small></p><p><strong>Measures of Central Tendency and Range - Question 36</strong></p><p>A class recorded the following number of absentees in five days: 3, 5, 4, 6 and 2. What was the mean number of absentees per day?</p>', 'Medium', 'JSS2/JSS3', '', 'Word Problem', '(3 + 5 + 4 + 6 + 2) ÷ 5 = 20 ÷ 5 = 4.', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 10:32:10', NULL, 0, 0),
(796, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 17, '<p><small>Source: Measures of Central Tendency and Range Topic Bank - Item 37</small></p><p><strong>Measures of Central Tendency and Range - Question 37</strong></p><p>The data set 10, 10, 11, 12, 50 contains an extreme value. Which measure gives a better idea of the typical value?</p>', 'Medium', 'JSS2/JSS3', '', 'Data Interpretation', 'The median is less affected by the extreme value 50 than the mean.', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 10:32:10', NULL, 0, 0),
(797, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 17, '<p><small>Source: Measures of Central Tendency and Range Topic Bank - Item 38</small></p><p><strong>Measures of Central Tendency and Range - Question 38</strong></p><p>The table shows the number of children in some families. Children: 1 2 3 4 Frequency: 2 6 5 1 What is the modal number of children?</p>', 'Medium', 'JSS2/JSS3', '', 'Frequency Table', 'The highest frequency is 6, corresponding to 2 children.', 'approved', 0, 2, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 10:32:10', NULL, 0, 0),
(798, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 17, '<p><small>Source: Measures of Central Tendency and Range Topic Bank - Item 39</small></p><p><strong>Measures of Central Tendency and Range - Question 39</strong></p><p>For the data 4, 6, 6, 8, 10, find the median and mode respectively.</p>', 'Medium', 'JSS2/JSS3', '', 'Mixed Measures', 'The middle value is 6, so the median is 6. The most frequent value is also 6.', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 10:32:10', NULL, 0, 0),
(799, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 17, '<p><small>Source: Measures of Central Tendency and Range Topic Bank - Item 40</small></p><p><strong>Measures of Central Tendency and Range - Question 40</strong></p><p>A student found the mean of 5, 10, 15 and 20 as 50. What mistake did the student most likely make?</p>', 'Medium', 'JSS2/JSS3', '', 'Error Detection', 'The sum is 50, but the mean is 50 ÷ 4 = 12.5.', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 10:32:10', NULL, 0, 0),
(800, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 17, '<p><small>Source: Measures of Central Tendency and Range Topic Bank - Item 41</small></p><p><strong>Measures of Central Tendency and Range - Question 41</strong></p><p>The table shows the scores of students. Score: 10 20 30 40 Frequency: 2 3 4 1 Find the mean score.</p>', 'Medium', 'JSS2/JSS3', '', 'Frequency Table', 'Total score = 10×2 + 20×3 + 30×4 + 40×1 = 240. Total frequency = 10. Mean = 240 ÷ 10 = 24.', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 10:32:10', NULL, 0, 0),
(801, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 17, '<p><small>Source: Measures of Central Tendency and Range Topic Bank - Item 42</small></p><p><strong>Measures of Central Tendency and Range - Question 42</strong></p><p>The mean of six numbers is 18. If one number, 30, is removed, the mean of the remaining five numbers is</p>', 'Medium', 'JSS2/JSS3', '', 'Mean', 'Original total = 18 × 6 = 108. New total = 108 − 30 = 78. New mean = 78 ÷ 5 = 15.6.', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 10:32:10', NULL, 0, 0),
(802, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 17, '<p><small>Source: Measures of Central Tendency and Range Topic Bank - Item 43</small></p><p><strong>Measures of Central Tendency and Range - Question 43</strong></p><p>The median of 4, 6, 8, x and 12 is 8. Which value of x makes the statement true?</p>', 'Medium', 'JSS2/JSS3', '', 'Median', 'If x = 9, the ordered data are 4, 6, 8, 9, 12. The middle value is 8.', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 10:32:10', NULL, 0, 0),
(803, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 17, '<p><small>Source: Measures of Central Tendency and Range Topic Bank - Item 44</small></p><p><strong>Measures of Central Tendency and Range - Question 44</strong></p><p>Which of the following data sets has no mode?</p>', 'Medium', 'JSS2/JSS3', '', 'Mode', 'In 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, no value occurs more than once.', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 10:32:10', NULL, 0, 0),
(804, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 17, '<p><small>Source: Measures of Central Tendency and Range Topic Bank - Item 45</small></p><p><strong>Measures of Central Tendency and Range - Question 45</strong></p><p>The range of a data set is 18. If the smallest value is 7, what is the largest value?</p>', 'Medium', 'JSS2/JSS3', '', 'Range', 'Range = Largest − Smallest. Largest = 18 + 7 = 25.', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 10:32:10', NULL, 0, 0),
(805, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 17, '<p><small>Source: Measures of Central Tendency and Range Topic Bank - Item 46</small></p><p><strong>Measures of Central Tendency and Range - Question 46</strong></p><p>A student scored 62, 70, 68, 75 and 80 in five tests. What is the mean score?</p>', 'Medium', 'JSS2/JSS3', '', 'Word Problem', 'Mean = (62 + 70 + 68 + 75 + 80) ÷ 5 = 355 ÷ 5 = 71.', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 10:32:10', NULL, 0, 0),
(806, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 17, '<p><small>Source: Measures of Central Tendency and Range Topic Bank - Item 47</small></p><p><strong>Measures of Central Tendency and Range - Question 47</strong></p><p>Two pupils have the same mean score, but one pupil has a larger range. What does the larger range show?</p>', 'Medium', 'JSS2/JSS3', '', 'Data Interpretation', 'A larger range shows a wider spread between the highest and lowest values.', 'approved', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 10:32:10', NULL, 0, 0),
(807, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 17, '<p><small>Source: Measures of Central Tendency and Range Topic Bank - Item 48</small></p><p><strong>Measures of Central Tendency and Range - Question 48</strong></p><p>The table shows the number of pencils owned by students. Pencils: 1 2 3 4 5 Frequency: 1 3 5 4 2 What is the mode?</p>', 'Medium', 'JSS2/JSS3', '', 'Frequency Table', 'The highest frequency is 5, corresponding to 3 pencils.', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 10:32:10', NULL, 0, 0),
(808, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 17, '<p><small>Source: Measures of Central Tendency and Range Topic Bank - Item 49</small></p><p><strong>Measures of Central Tendency and Range - Question 49</strong></p><p>For the data 3, 5, 5, 7 and 10, find the mean and mode respectively.</p>', 'Medium', 'JSS2/JSS3', '', 'Mixed Measures', 'Mean = (3 + 5 + 5 + 7 + 10) ÷ 5 = 30 ÷ 5 = 6. Mode = 5.', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 10:32:10', NULL, 0, 0),
(809, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 17, '<p><small>Source: Measures of Central Tendency and Range Topic Bank - Item 50</small></p><p><strong>Measures of Central Tendency and Range - Question 50</strong></p><p>A student says the mode of 2, 4, 4, 6, 6, 8 is 4 only. What is wrong with the answer?</p>', 'Medium', 'JSS2/JSS3', '', 'Error Detection', 'Both 4 and 6 occur twice, so the data is bimodal.', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 10:32:10', NULL, 0, 0),
(810, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 17, '<p><small>Source: Measures of Central Tendency and Range Topic Bank - Item 51</small></p><p><strong>Measures of Central Tendency and Range - Question 51</strong></p><p>Find the median of 32, 28, 35, 30, 40, 38, 34 and 36.</p>', 'Medium', 'JSS2/JSS3', '', 'Median', 'Ordered data: 28, 30, 32, 34, 35, 36, 38, 40. Median = (34 + 35) ÷ 2 = 34.5.', 'approved', 0, 2, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 10:32:10', NULL, 0, 0),
(811, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 17, '<p><small>Source: Measures of Central Tendency and Range Topic Bank - Item 52</small></p><p><strong>Measures of Central Tendency and Range - Question 52</strong></p><p>The mean of four numbers is 16. Three of the numbers are 12, 18 and 20. Find the fourth number.</p>', 'Medium', 'JSS2/JSS3', '', 'Mean', 'Total = 16 × 4 = 64. Sum of known values = 50. Fourth number = 64 − 50 = 14.', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 10:32:10', NULL, 0, 0),
(812, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 17, '<p><small>Source: Measures of Central Tendency and Range Topic Bank - Item 53</small></p><p><strong>Measures of Central Tendency and Range - Question 53</strong></p><p>A data set has values 11, 15, 18, 20 and 24. If 24 is replaced by 30, what is the new range?</p>', 'Medium', 'JSS2/JSS3', '', 'Range', 'New range = 30 − 11 = 19.', 'approved', 0, 2, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 10:32:10', NULL, 0, 0),
(813, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 17, '<p><small>Source: Measures of Central Tendency and Range Topic Bank - Item 54</small></p><p><strong>Measures of Central Tendency and Range - Question 54</strong></p><p>Which measure is best used to identify the most popular shoe size among students?</p>', 'Medium', 'JSS2/JSS3', '', 'Data Interpretation', 'The most popular value is the value that occurs most often, which is the mode.', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 10:32:10', NULL, 0, 0),
(814, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 17, '<p><small>Source: Measures of Central Tendency and Range Topic Bank - Item 55</small></p><p><strong>Measures of Central Tendency and Range - Question 55</strong></p><p>The table shows the number of siblings of some students. Siblings: 0 1 2 3 Frequency: 3 5 4 2 Find the total number of students.</p>', 'Medium', 'JSS2/JSS3', '', 'Frequency Table', 'Total number of students = 3 + 5 + 4 + 2 = 14.', 'approved', 0, 2, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 10:32:10', NULL, 0, 0),
(815, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 17, '<p><small>Source: Measures of Central Tendency and Range Topic Bank - Item 56</small></p><p><strong>Measures of Central Tendency and Range - Question 56</strong></p><p>The mean of 8 numbers is 12. If one number is changed from 6 to 22, what is the new mean?</p>', 'Hard', 'JSS2/JSS3', '', 'Mean', 'Original total = 12 × 8 = 96. Increase = 22 − 6 = 16. New total = 112. New mean = 112 ÷ 8 = 14.', 'approved', 0, 2, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 10:32:10', NULL, 0, 0),
(816, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 17, '<p><small>Source: Measures of Central Tendency and Range Topic Bank - Item 57</small></p><p><strong>Measures of Central Tendency and Range - Question 57</strong></p><p>The median of 6, 8, x, 12 and 15 is 10. If the data are arranged in ascending order, find x.</p>', 'Hard', 'JSS2/JSS3', '', 'Median', 'For five ordered values, the median is the third value. Therefore, x = 10.', 'approved', 0, 2, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 10:32:10', NULL, 0, 0),
(817, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 17, '<p><small>Source: Measures of Central Tendency and Range Topic Bank - Item 58</small></p><p><strong>Measures of Central Tendency and Range - Question 58</strong></p><p>The table shows the scores of students. Score: 1 2 3 4 5 Frequency: 2 3 4 3 2 Find the mean score.</p>', 'Hard', 'JSS2/JSS3', '', 'Frequency Table', 'Total score = 1×2 + 2×3 + 3×4 + 4×3 + 5×2 = 42. Total frequency = 14. Mean = 42 ÷ 14 = 3.', 'approved', 0, 3, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 10:32:10', NULL, 0, 0),
(818, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 17, '<p><small>Source: Measures of Central Tendency and Range Topic Bank - Item 59</small></p><p><strong>Measures of Central Tendency and Range - Question 59</strong></p><p>For the data 4, 6, 6, 8, 10, 12, find the median, mode and range respectively.</p>', 'Hard', 'JSS2/JSS3', '', 'Mixed Measures', 'Median = (6 + 8) ÷ 2 = 7. Mode = 6. Range = 12 − 4 = 8.', 'approved', 0, 2, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 10:32:10', NULL, 0, 0),
(819, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 17, '<p><small>Source: Measures of Central Tendency and Range Topic Bank - Item 60</small></p><p><strong>Measures of Central Tendency and Range - Question 60</strong></p><p>A class has scores 20, 22, 23, 24, 25 and 80. Which statement is most correct?</p>', 'Hard', 'JSS2/JSS3', '', 'Data Interpretation', 'The extreme value 80 affects the mean and range strongly, but the median remains more representative of the typical score.', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 10:32:10', NULL, 0, 0),
(820, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 17, '<p><small>Source: Measures of Central Tendency and Range Topic Bank - Item 61</small></p><p><strong>Measures of Central Tendency and Range - Question 61</strong></p><p>The mean of 10 numbers is 18. If one of the numbers, 27, is omitted, the mean of the remaining numbers is 17. How many numbers remain after the omission?</p>', 'Hard', 'JSS2/JSS3', '', 'Mean', 'Original total = 18 × 10 = 180. After removing 27, the new total is 153. Since one number was removed from 10 numbers, 9 numbers remain, and 153 ÷ 9 = 17.', 'approved', 0, 2, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 10:32:10', NULL, 0, 0),
(821, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 17, '<p><small>Source: Measures of Central Tendency and Range Topic Bank - Item 62</small></p><p><strong>Measures of Central Tendency and Range - Question 62</strong></p><p>The table shows the number of books read by students. Books: 1 2 3 4 5 Frequency: 2 4 6 3 1 Find the median number of books read.</p>', 'Hard', 'JSS2/JSS3', '', 'Frequency Table', 'Total frequency = 16. The 8th and 9th observations both fall in the value 3, so the median is 3.', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 10:32:10', NULL, 0, 0),
(822, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 17, '<p><small>Source: Measures of Central Tendency and Range Topic Bank - Item 63</small></p><p><strong>Measures of Central Tendency and Range - Question 63</strong></p><p>A data set has exactly two modes. What is such a data set called?</p>', 'Hard', 'JSS2/JSS3', '', 'Mode', 'A data set with two modes is called bimodal.', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 10:32:10', NULL, 0, 0),
(823, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 17, '<p><small>Source: Measures of Central Tendency and Range Topic Bank - Item 64</small></p><p><strong>Measures of Central Tendency and Range - Question 64</strong></p><p>The range of a data set is 24. If every value in the data set is increased by 7, what is the new range?</p>', 'Hard', 'JSS2/JSS3', '', 'Range', 'Adding the same number to every observation does not change the range.', 'approved', 0, 2, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 10:32:10', NULL, 0, 0),
(824, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 17, '<p><small>Source: Measures of Central Tendency and Range Topic Bank - Item 65</small></p><p><strong>Measures of Central Tendency and Range - Question 65</strong></p><p>Two classes have the same mean examination score. Class A has a range of 8, while Class B has a range of 22. What can be concluded?</p>', 'Hard', 'JSS2/JSS3', '', 'Data Interpretation', 'A larger range indicates greater variation in the scores.', 'approved', 0, 3, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 10:32:10', NULL, 0, 0),
(825, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 17, '<p><small>Source: Measures of Central Tendency and Range Topic Bank - Item 66</small></p><p><strong>Measures of Central Tendency and Range - Question 66</strong></p><p>The mean of five numbers is 16. Four of the numbers are 11, 15, 18 and 20. What is the fifth number?</p>', 'Hard', 'JSS2/JSS3', '', 'Mean', 'Total = 16 × 5 = 80. Sum of known numbers = 64. Fifth number = 80 − 64 = 16.', 'approved', 0, 2, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 10:32:10', NULL, 0, 0),
(826, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 17, '<p><small>Source: Measures of Central Tendency and Range Topic Bank - Item 67</small></p><p><strong>Measures of Central Tendency and Range - Question 67</strong></p><p>A student claims that adding the same number to every observation changes the range. Which statement is correct?</p>', 'Hard', 'JSS2/JSS3', '', 'Error Detection', 'Since both the largest and smallest values increase by the same amount, their difference remains unchanged.', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 10:32:10', NULL, 0, 0),
(827, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 17, '<p><small>Source: Measures of Central Tendency and Range Topic Bank - Item 68</small></p><p><strong>Measures of Central Tendency and Range - Question 68</strong></p><p>The table shows students&#039; scores. Score: 2 4 6 8 Frequency: 1 3 5 1 Which score is the median?</p>', 'Hard', 'JSS2/JSS3', '', 'Frequency Table', 'There are 10 observations. The 5th and 6th observations are both 6, so the median is 6.', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 10:32:10', NULL, 0, 0),
(828, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 17, '<p><small>Source: Measures of Central Tendency and Range Topic Bank - Item 69</small></p><p><strong>Measures of Central Tendency and Range - Question 69</strong></p><p>For the data set 5, 7, 8, 8, 10, 13 and 20, which pair of measures is equal?</p>', 'Hard', 'JSS2/JSS3', '', 'Mixed Measures', 'Median = 8 and mode = 8. Mean = 71 ÷ 7 ≈ 10.14 and range = 20 - 5 = 15. Therefore, the median and mode are equal.', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 10:32:10', NULL, 0, 0),
(829, 1, 0, 'topic', 0, 17, '<p><small>Source: Measures of Central Tendency and Range Topic Bank - Item 70</small></p><p><strong>Measures of Central Tendency and Range - Question 70</strong></p><p>A school wants to know the shoe size most commonly worn by JSS3 students so that enough sports shoes can be ordered. Which measure should be used?</p>', 'Hard', 'JSS2/JSS3', '', 'Application', 'The mode identifies the most frequently occurring shoe size.', 'approved', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-06-18 10:32:10', NULL, 0, 0);
